UID:beinecke-short-term-fellowships-2027-2028@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260831T203817Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260815
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260816
SUMMARY:Deadline: Beinecke Library Short-Term Research Fellowships 2027-202
 8 (Yale)
DESCRIPTION:The Beinecke Library Fellowship Program offers competitive shor
 t-term fellowships to support research projects that substantively engage 
 with Yale Library Special Collections materials. WHO CAN APPLY: academic a
 nd independent scholars\, locally and globally\, with or without an instit
 utional affiliation\; the library explicitly welcomes applicants regardles
 s of institutional association\, race\, cultural background\, ability\, se
 xual orientation\, gender or socioeconomic status. Applications using trad
 itional archival and bibliographic research methods are encouraged\, and s
 o are creative\, interdisciplinary and non-traditional approaches to worki
 ng with the collections\, which makes this a live option for artists and w
 riters whose practice is research-driven. WHAT YOU GET: USD 5\,000 per mon
 th for an onsite research visit of between two weeks and two months\, paid
  at the start of the fellowship whenever possible (international fellows s
 hould expect payment to take several weeks)\; fellows pay their own taxes 
 on the award. TIMELINE: applications for the 2027-2028 awards opened 1 Jun
 e 2026 and close 15 August 2026\, via Interfolio\; all decisions are notif
 ied by 31 January 2027\; research must be conducted between 1 July 2027 an
 d 30 June 2028\, and awards cannot be deferred.\n\nOrganisation: Beinecke 
 Rare Book & Manuscript Library\, Yale University\nLocation: Onsite at Yale
  Library Special Collections\, New Haven\, Connecticut\, USA. Open to acad
 emic and independent scholars locally and globally\, regardless of institu
 tional association.\nAward: USD 5\,000 per month for research visits betwe
 en two weeks and two months. Funding is paid at the beginning of the fello
 wship where possible (payment to international fellows often takes several
  weeks)\; fellows are responsible for taxes on the award. Free to apply.\n
 Duration: Two weeks to two months of onsite research\, conducted between 1
  July 2027 and 30 June 2028\; awards cannot be deferred\n\nMore: https://b
 einecke.library.yale.edu/beinecke/researchers/fellowships/short-term?utm_s
 ource=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://beinecke.library.yale.edu/beinecke/researchers/fellowships/shor
 t-term?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Onsite at Yale Library Special Collections\, New Haven\, Connectic
 ut\, USA. Open to academic and independent scholars locally and globally\,
  regardless of institutional association.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:knowcase-sonar-cotec-open-call-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260831T203817Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260907
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260908
SUMMARY:Deadline: KNOWCASE Open Call 2027: permanent digital-culture instal
 lation in Madrid (Sonar+D x Fundacion Cotec)
DESCRIPTION:Fundacion Cotec (a Spanish innovation-focused non-profit) and S
 onar+D\, building on an initial experiment at Sonar 2026\, invite proposal
 s for a long-term installation at KNOWCASE\, the street-level showcase of 
 Cotec's Madrid headquarters in Chamberi\, visible to the public 24 hours a
  day. THEME: digital culture\, meaning projects that combine knowledge\, r
 esearch\, science and data with art\, technology and social impact. Cotec'
 s stated priorities are the big transitions (analogue to digital\, linear 
 to circular economy\, tangible to intangible) plus innovation ecosystems a
 nd R&D&I\, the climate crisis\, the future of work and learning\, social d
 ivides\, citizen participation and democratic health. WHAT YOU GET: a budg
 et of up to EUR 100\,000 plus VAT covering everything (design\, production
 \, installation\, maintenance\, documentation\, artist fees\, travel\, acc
 ommodation and insurance)\, and a minimum 24-month public display from Feb
 ruary 2027. WHO CAN APPLY: artists\, collectives\, designers\, technologis
 ts\, universities\, research centres\, startups\, businesses\, creative ag
 encies\, producers\, cultural institutions and multidisciplinary teams\, i
 nternationally\; applicants must demonstrate solid experience and a releva
 nt portfolio. CONSTRAINTS: the proposal must be original and never previou
 sly exhibited\, must include participative or interactive elements\, must 
 encourage critical thinking\, and must be technically and financially viab
 le for the full 24+ month exhibition period (durability and maintenance ar
 e central selection criteria). Selection weighs conceptual quality highest
  (40 percent)\, followed by public interactivity (25 percent). HOW TO APPL
 Y: one PDF of maximum 15 pages containing summary\, concept\, technical pr
 oposal\, visuals\, budget\, timeline\, team profile\, portfolio and declar
 ation\, in Spanish\, another official language of Spain\, or English\, via
  the application portal linked from the terms and conditions. Results anno
 unced 14 October 2026. Deadline 7 September 2026 at midnight CEST.\n\nOrga
 nisation: Fundacion Cotec and Sonar+D\nLocation: Installation at the KNOWC
 ASE storefront of Fundacion Cotec's headquarters in Chamberi\, Madrid\, Sp
 ain\, a street-level venue visible 24/7. The call is international\; appli
 cations accepted in Spanish\, other official languages of Spain\, or Engli
 sh.\nAward: Up to EUR 100\,000 (plus VAT)\, all-inclusive: conceptualisati
 on\, design\, technical development\, production\, installation\, maintena
 nce\, documentation\, artist fees\, travel\, accommodation and insurance.\
 nDuration: Installation displayed for a minimum of 24 months\, starting Fe
 bruary 2027\n\nMore: https://sonar.es/en/news/knowcase-open-call-2027?utm_
 source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://sonar.es/en/news/knowcase-open-call-2027?utm_source=artificialn
 ouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Installation at the KNOWCASE storefront of Fundacion Cotec's headq
 uarters in Chamberi\, Madrid\, Spain\, a street-level venue visible 24/7. 
 The call is international\; applications accepted in Spanish\, other offic
 ial languages of Spain\, or English.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:studio-alta-residence-2027-open-calls@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260831T203817Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260910
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260911
SUMMARY:Deadline: Studio ALTA Residence 2027: four residency open calls (Pr
 ague)
DESCRIPTION:Prague performance venue Studio ALTA announces four residency o
 pen calls for 2027\, all with a single deadline of 10 September 2026. RESE
 ARCH HOUSE (19 to 28 April 2027): a shared residential laboratory for thre
 e art projects or individual artists in the early stages of exploration an
 d experimentation\, or reopening an existing finished work (performance\, 
 installation\, object\, video) to transform it into another form such as a
  workshop\, text or performance-lecture. Includes a 10-day residency\, a f
 ee of CZK 12\,000 per project\, shared studio\, individual workspace and f
 acilitated exchange meetings\; the research output must be shared publicly
  as a work-in-progress in a form based on participants' needs. REST HOUSE 
 (March to November 2027): a five-day residential spa for overloaded collea
 gues from the arts sector\, with no required output or activities\; restri
 cted to people working in production\, dramaturgy\, curation\, PR\, techni
 cal and other supporting artistic professions in the Czech independent sec
 tor. Two guests are chosen by lottery (fee CZK 6\,000 per person)\; the pu
 blic draw is announced 16 September 2026. HOUSE IN THE NEIGHBORHOOD (9 to 
 18 August 2027): for one performative art project created with the local c
 ommunity and designed or adapted for public space in Liben and its surroun
 dings\; this year's call focuses on the 55+ target group. Includes a fee o
 f CZK 30\,000 per project\, rehearsal and indoor facilities (primarily out
 door spaces)\, dramaturgic\, production\, technical and PR consultation\, 
 connections to partner organisations\, and 7 days of intensive production 
 and technical support in the final phase. A public premiere or work-in-pro
 gress in public space at the end of the residency is required. HOUSE OF SW
 EAT (1 to 10 February 2027): for one performative art project designed or 
 adapted for the specific environment of the Studio ALTA sauna and its imme
 diate surroundings\, seeking new ways of working with intimate space\, pro
 ximity to the audience and non-traditional formats. Includes a fee of CZK 
 15\,000 per project\, a 10-day residency\, sauna and rehearsal spaces\, dr
 amaturgic\, production\, technical and PR consultation\, and 2 days of int
 ensive final-phase support\; a public work-in-progress or premiere in the 
 sauna within the 9 to 12 February 2027 programme block is required. Projec
 ts at any stage of development can apply to the production calls\, and sel
 ected projects may be included in Studio ALTA's year-round programme. TIME
 LINE: deadline 10 September 2026\; results 3 weeks after the deadline (30 
 September 2026)\; a Q&A Zoom call takes place 10 August 2026 at 3:00 PM. A
 pply via the registration forms on the call page.\n\nOrganisation: Studio 
 ALTA\nLocation: Studio ALTA\, Prague (Liben district)\, Czech Republic. Th
 ree of the four calls are open internationally\; the Rest House call is re
 served for supporting-profession arts workers active in the Czech independ
 ent sector.\nAward: Residency fees paid to participants: Research House CZ
 K 12\,000 per project\; Rest House CZK 6\,000 per person\; House in the Ne
 ighborhood CZK 30\,000 per project\; House of Sweat CZK 15\,000 per projec
 t. All include workspace at Studio ALTA\; the two production residencies a
 dd dramaturgic\, production\, technical and PR support. Free to apply.\nDu
 ration: Programme dependent: 5 to 10 days\, at various points between Febr
 uary and November 2027\n\nMore: https://www.altart.cz/rezidence-2027/?utm_
 source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.altart.cz/rezidence-2027/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrant
 desk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Studio ALTA\, Prague (Liben district)\, Czech Republic. Three of t
 he four calls are open internationally\; the Rest House call is reserved f
 or supporting-profession arts workers active in the Czech independent sect
 or.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:cpr-artist-in-residence-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260831T203817Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260824
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260825
SUMMARY:Deadline: CPR Center for Performance Research: Artist-in-Residence 
 Program 2027
DESCRIPTION:CPR's year-long Artist-in-Residence programme supports six New 
 York City-based artists working across contemporary dance\, performance an
 d time-based art. The organisation values experimental approaches to conte
 nt\, form and aesthetics and explicitly encourages risk-taking\, interdisc
 iplinarity and the unexpected\, so process-led and hard-to-categorise work
  is in scope rather than a liability. WHAT RESIDENTS RECEIVE: a $2\,000 st
 ipend\; 20 free hours of rehearsal space plus up to 150 further subsidised
  hours in CPR's two studios\, with priority and advance calendar access\; 
 participation in OPEN LAB (facilitated embodied workshops and feedback sho
 wings) and OPEN AiR (solo or shared presentations of current work)\; and a
 ccess to technical equipment and production support. ELIGIBILITY: artists 
 must be based in New York City and remain so throughout the cycle (no visa
  sponsorship)\; must have had work publicly presented before\; must not ha
 ve held a CPR residency in the last five years\; and current undergraduate
 s are not eligible. Individuals\, companies\, collaboratives and collectiv
 es may all apply\, each counting as a single residency. CPR strongly encou
 rages applications from BIPOC\, LGBTQ+\, immigrant and disabled artists an
 d from artists across generations. APPLICATION: a Google Form with narrati
 ve answers on the artist's central research focus and its alignment with C
 PR's values\; drafting answers in a separate document first is recommended
 . Selection is by an independent panel of artists\, curators and arts lead
 ers. Deadline: Monday 24 August 2026 at 5pm ET\; late submissions are not 
 accepted. Notifications November 2026. Questions: applications@cprnyc.org.
 \n\nOrganisation: CPR - Center for Performance Research\nLocation: Brookly
 n\, New York City\, USA. RESTRICTED: NYC-based artists only\; CPR does not
  sponsor visas\, and residents must remain NYC-based for the whole cycle.\
 nAward: $2\,000 stipend\, 20 free hours of rehearsal space\, up to 150 sub
 sidised rehearsal hours across CPR's two studios with priority and advance
  booking\, presentation slots in the OPEN LAB and OPEN AiR programmes\, an
 d access to technical equipment and production support. No application fee
 .\nDuration: One year\, January to December 2027\n\nMore: https://www.cprn
 yc.org/events/opencall-2027airprogram?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdes
 k&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.cprnyc.org/events/opencall-2027airprogram?utm_source=artifi
 cialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Brooklyn\, New York City\, USA. RESTRICTED: NYC-based artists only
 \; CPR does not sponsor visas\, and residents must remain NYC-based for th
 e whole cycle.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:surface-design-association-air-2026-27@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260831T203817Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260814
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260815
SUMMARY:Deadline: Surface Design Association: Artist in Residence 2026-27 (
 virtual)
DESCRIPTION:The Surface Design Association's Artist in Residence programme 
 is built to develop skills\, open up relationships and support fiber and t
 extile artists through a studio project that pushes their practice. The re
 sidency is entirely virtual and runs across a full year\, which is the poi
 nt: it removes the travel\, housing and time-away barriers that keep many 
 practitioners out of in-person residencies. One artist is selected annuall
 y by a panel of SDA staff\, board members and committee volunteers. WHAT I
 T INVOLVES: studio visits across the year\, social media programming\, and
  meetings with the SDA community\, plus further programming shaped around 
 the resident's own skills and interests\, which can include teaching onlin
 e workshops\, contributing to SDA publications\, jurying exhibitions or jo
 ining panels. FUNDING: a $2\,000 studio stipend for the project\, plus up 
 to $2\,000 in additional compensation for programming work\, targeting abo
 ut $4\,000 total. ELIGIBILITY: emerging\, mid-career and established artis
 ts\; US-based and international applicants welcome\; students and professi
 onals may apply\; applicants must hold current SDA membership (from $85 pe
 r year\, $60 for students). APPLICATION: a portfolio of 10 images with ful
 l artwork information (title\, year\, materials\, technique\, dimensions\,
  photo credit)\, a detailed CV\, essay responses on artistic goals\, progr
 amming interests and professional development\, and demographic informatio
 n. No application fee. The 2026-27 cycle closes 14 August 2026.\n\nOrganis
 ation: Surface Design Association (SDA)\nLocation: Fully virtual. Open to 
 US-based and international applicants\; current SDA membership is required
 .\nAward: $2\,000 studio stipend\, plus up to $2\,000 further compensation
  for programming work (SDA aims for roughly $4\,000 in total per resident)
 . No application fee\, but applicants must be current SDA members (members
 hip from $85 per year\, $60 for students).\nDuration: One year\, virtual\,
  October 2026 to August 2027\n\nMore: https://www.surfacedesign.org/air_fo
 rm/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.surfacedesign.org/air_form/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugra
 ntdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Fully virtual. Open to US-based and international applicants\; cur
 rent SDA membership is required.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:bigci-environmental-awards-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260831T203817Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260802
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260803
SUMMARY:Deadline: BigCi Environmental Awards 2026
DESCRIPTION:BigCi's Environmental Awards are an annual prize for work that 
 engages with the environment\, open to Australian and international artist
 s working in visual art\, installation\, multimedia\, performance\, litera
 ture\, music\, photography\, filmmaking and curating. TWO WINNERS each rec
 eive four weeks of free residency at BigCi plus AUD 5\,000 in prize money.
  BigCi sits on the edge of Wollemi National Park in the Greater Blue Mount
 ains\, an hour and a half from Sydney but geologically another world\; win
 ners explore the UNESCO World Heritage-listed Wollemi\, Blue Mountains and
  Gardens of Stone National Parks on guided walks and are given research as
 sistance relevant to their projects. At the end of their residencies they 
 present the work at the BigCi Open Day. JUDGING: three independent judges\
 , Lea Kannar-Lichtenberger (Australia)\, Brian Wallace (China) and Dan Got
 tlieb (USA). APPLICATION: an online submission form (Wufoo) linked from th
 e awards page\, with a non-refundable AUD 40 entry fee paid at the time of
  submission. KEY DATES: submissions close 2 August 2026\; winners announce
 d 22 August 2026. Enquiries via the contact form at bigci.org/contact.\n\n
 Organisation: Bilpin International Ground for Creative Initiatives (BigCi)
 \nLocation: Bilpin\, New South Wales\, Australia\, on the edge of Wollemi 
 National Park in the UNESCO World Heritage-listed Greater Blue Mountains\,
  about 1.5 hours from Sydney. Open to Australian and international artists
 .\nAward: Two awards\, each of AUD 5\,000 prize money plus four weeks of f
 ree residency at BigCi\, guided walks in the surrounding national parks an
 d research assistance for the project. AUD 40 entry fee\, non-refundable a
 nd payable with the submission.\nDuration: Four-week residency at BigCi pe
 r winner\n\nMore: https://bigci.org/awards/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugr
 antdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://bigci.org/awards/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_med
 ium=referral
LOCATION:Bilpin\, New South Wales\, Australia\, on the edge of Wollemi Nati
 onal Park in the UNESCO World Heritage-listed Greater Blue Mountains\, abo
 ut 1.5 hours from Sydney. Open to Australian and international artists.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:latitude-air-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260831T203817Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260901
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260902
SUMMARY:Deadline: LATITUDE Artist in Residence 2027 (Chicago)
DESCRIPTION:The LATITUDE Artist in Residence program (started in 2013) is a
  one-month production residency where 8-10 artists are granted full access
  to LATITUDE's facilities and community to develop their practice. Its foc
 us is supporting artists who want to use LATITUDE's printing and scanning 
 services to expand their practice\, regardless of medium or experience\; p
 ast residents include photographers\, painters\, performance artists\, new
  media artists\, and sculptors. WHAT RESIDENTS RECEIVE: a $1\,000 printing
  stipend\, unlimited scanning\, a personal studio with a calibrated workst
 ation and 24/7 access\, training and guidance on tech from staff\, an orga
 nised public event to present new work\, and lifetime free lab access. LAT
 ITUDE does not offer a housing stipend but will help schedule studio visit
 s during the month. PUBLIC PROGRAMMING: during the residency each artist p
 uts on one community programming event (past examples include panel discus
 sions\, artist talks\, performances\, workshops\, and critiques\; a galler
 y space is available for curation) and is asked to act as a mentor to the 
 community\, sharing insights and creative methods. WHO SHOULD APPLY: artis
 ts interested in production\, education\, and tech experimentation\; no pr
 ior printing experience\, art education\, or media specificity is required
 \, though professionalism and communication are expected. 2027 PANEL COMMI
 TTEE: Yechen Zhao\, B. Ingrid Olson\, Teri Carson. TIMELINE: applications 
 open 1 August 2026 (free before 16 August\, a $20 donation thereafter) and
  close 1 September 2026 at 12pm (noon) CST\; the selection committee revie
 ws in September\, meets to decide finalists in October\, and acceptances a
 re sent early November 2026. Apply at latitudechicago.org/artist-in-reside
 nce.\n\nOrganisation: LATITUDE Chicago\nLocation: Chicago\, Illinois\, USA
 . No housing stipend offered.\nAward: One-month production residency for 8
 -10 artists: a $1\,000 printing stipend\, unlimited scanning\, a personal 
 studio with a calibrated workstation\, staff training and guidance on tech
 \, an organised public event\, and lifetime free lab access. No housing st
 ipend. Free to apply before 16 August 2026\; a $20 donation thereafter.\nD
 uration: One month (residency takes place in 2027)\n\nMore: https://www.la
 titudechicago.org/artist-in-residence?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdes
 k&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.latitudechicago.org/artist-in-residence?utm_source=artifici
 alnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Chicago\, Illinois\, USA. No housing stipend offered.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:onview-artist-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260831T203817Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260907
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260908
SUMMARY:Deadline: ON::View Artist Residency Program 2027 (Savannah\, Georgi
 a)
DESCRIPTION:Located in the heart of Savannah's Starland District at ARTS So
 utheast\, the fully-funded ON::View Artist Residency provides a free\, hig
 h-visibility studio space\, lodging\, and a $500 stipend for an artist or 
 curator to complete a new project\, continue an in-progress endeavour\, or
  conduct research. The studio's large east-facing street-level windows loo
 k onto Bull Street\, allowing the resident's work to be on view to the com
 munity 24/7 as visitors and passersby witness the process from concept to 
 final execution. It is the only residency of its kind in Savannah and welc
 omes creatives from around the globe working in all media. STUDIO: 12 x 12
  feet just off the ARTS Southeast lobby\, with 24-hour access\; residents 
 must work during public open hours (Thursday to Sunday\, 12 to 5PM) a mini
 mum of one day per week\, and must be present during the First Friday Prog
 ram Finale. Restrictions: no aerosol or toxic/high-VOC materials\, no ongo
 ing or repetitive loud noise (occasional hand and power tool use is allowe
 d)\; accepted applicants provide their own materials and supplies. LODGING
 : the 5th Dimension Apartment a few blocks away\, a cozy studio with full 
 kitchen and bath\, private gated entrance and garden\, wifi and TV\, queen
  bed\; houses up to 2 people (larger teams should arrange additional housi
 ng). No smoking or pets. ENGAGEMENT: residents do an Instagram takeover vi
 a @onviewresidency\, are encouraged to give a public lecture\, workshop\, 
 or interactive event\, and may participate in an annual group exhibition i
 n February 2028. ELIGIBILITY: creatives in all media\; collaborative teams
  are eligible (one proposal per team)\; current Studio Members or those wh
 o were Studio Members in the last 6 months are not eligible. Creatives may
  seek additional funding from other organisations\, and ARTS Southeast wil
 l provide a letter of support to accepted residents seeking grants. KEY DA
 TES: deadline Monday 7 September 2026 by 11:59PM\; first-round notificatio
 ns 18 September 2026\; interviews 21 to 25 September 2026\; final notifica
 tions 12 October 2026. APPLICATION: pay the $50 application fee (waivable 
 at ARTS Southeast's discretion for undue burden)\, then complete the onlin
 e application. Supported in part by the Georgia Council for the Arts\, the
  National Endowment for the Arts\, and the City of Savannah.\n\nOrganisati
 on: ARTS Southeast\nLocation: Starland District\, Savannah\, Georgia\, USA
 . Open to creatives from around the globe.\nAward: Fully funded: free high
 -visibility studio space\, free lodging at the 5th Dimension Apartment\, a
 nd a $500 stipend (for travel\, materials\, or any use). $50 application f
 ee\, waivable at the organisation's discretion if it is an undue burden.\n
 Duration: February to May 2027\n\nMore: https://artssoutheast.org/onview-r
 esidency-app?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://artssoutheast.org/onview-residency-app?utm_source=artificialnou
 veaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Starland District\, Savannah\, Georgia\, USA. Open to creatives fr
 om around the globe.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:designto-yonge-st-clair-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260831T203817Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260913
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260914
SUMMARY:Deadline: Call for Proposals: Activate Yonge + St. Clair During Des
 ignTO Festival 2027 (Toronto)
DESCRIPTION:Artists\, architects\, designers\, fabricators\, and multidisci
 plinary creatives are invited to submit proposals for a series of site-spe
 cific installations at Yonge + St. Clair as part of DesignTO Festival 2027
 . For more than seven years the Yonge + St. Clair BIA has partnered with D
 esignTO to transform publicly accessible spaces throughout the neighbourho
 od into an exhibition of art\, design\, and placemaking. For the 2027 Fest
 ival\, SEVEN installation opportunities are available across lobbies\, gal
 leries\, and window spaces: 2 St. Clair Ave W (Lobby)\, 2 St. Clair Ave E 
 (Lower Level Window)\, 30 St. Clair Ave W (Lobby)\, 40 St. Clair Ave W (Lo
 bby)\, 55 St. Clair Ave W (Lobby)\, 95 St. Clair Ave W (Gallery)\, and 152
 1 Yonge St (Window). One installation will be commissioned per location. T
 HEME: 'Intersections' - proposals may explore convergence\, transformation
 \, movement\, identity\, exchange\, and the evolving relationship between 
 people and place. Artists may submit proposals for multiple locations\, bu
 t each proposal must be tailored to its site and submitted separately\; on
 ly one proposal per artist or team may be selected. WHO SHOULD APPLY: emer
 ging and established artists\, designers\, architects\, fabricators\, and 
 multidisciplinary creative practitioners working in any medium\; preferenc
 e given to artists based in Toronto and the Greater Toronto Area. BUDGET: 
 selected projects receive $5\,000 to $7\,500 CAD inclusive of artist fees\
 , materials\, fabrication\, transportation\, installation\, and de-install
 ation. Artists are responsible for the fabrication\, transportation\, inst
 allation\, and de-installation of their work. KEY DATES: submission deadli
 ne 13 September 2026 at 5:00pm ET\; selected artists notified late Septemb
 er 2026\; final project information due October 2026\; installation period
  14 to 21 January 2027\; DesignTO Festival exhibition 22 to 31 January 202
 7\; de-installation 1 to 2 February 2027. HOW TO APPLY: submit a single PD
 F (artist information and biography\, project description and executive su
 mmary\, visual materials\, detailed line-item budget\, and current resume)
  via email or Dropbox link to info@yongestclair.ca with the subject line '
 DesignTO Festival 2027 - Installation Name - Artist Name'. Free to apply.\
 n\nOrganisation: DesignTO\nLocation: Yonge + St. Clair\, Toronto\, Canada.
  Preference given to artists based in Toronto and the Greater Toronto Area
 .\nAward: Between $5\,000 and $7\,500 CAD per selected project\, inclusive
  of artist fees\, materials\, fabrication\, transportation\, installation\
 , and de-installation. Free to apply.\nDuration: Installation presented du
 ring DesignTO Festival 2027\, 22 to 31 January 2027 (install 14 to 21 Janu
 ary\, de-install 1 to 2 February)\n\nMore: https://designto.org/blog/call-
 for-proposals-activate-yonge-st-clair-during-designto-festival-2027/?utm_s
 ource=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://designto.org/blog/call-for-proposals-activate-yonge-st-clair-du
 ring-designto-festival-2027/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_med
 ium=referral
LOCATION:Yonge + St. Clair\, Toronto\, Canada. Preference given to artists 
 based in Toronto and the Greater Toronto Area.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:gmap-digital-art-culture-lab-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260831T203817Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260809
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260810
SUMMARY:Deadline: G.MAP Digital Art Culture Lab 2026: Project Lab (Gwangju\
 , South Korea)
DESCRIPTION:The Gwangju Media Art Platform (G.MAP)\, an institution of Gwan
 gju\, UNESCO Creative City of Media Arts\, invites artists and teams worki
 ng in digital art to the 2026 Digital Art Culture Lab: Project Lab\, a fiv
 e-month creation support program (August to December 2026) covering the en
 tire creative process from idea development through production\, showcase 
 and archiving. WHO CAN APPLY: artists and groups in digital art wishing to
  create interdisciplinary projects using digital technology (all members a
 ged 19+\; international applicants welcome). Focus areas: digital art\, me
 dia art\, generative art\, AI\, interactive art\, XR\, AR\, VR\, interdisc
 iplinary\, art and technology. SELECTION: 14 teams total across two tracks
 : Track 1 Digital Transformation (7 artists/teams) and Track 2 Interdiscip
 linary Creation (7 teams). INTERNATIONAL ARTISTS CAN APPLY FOR TRACK 2 ONL
 Y. SUPPORT: creation and production grant up to KRW 30\,000\,000 per team 
 for Track 2\, two online mentoring sessions\, and a showcase in G.MAP exhi
 bition spaces and on large-scale public media platforms including the G.MA
 P LED Wall and city media facades. KEY DATES: application period 21 July t
 o 9 August 2026\, 6 PM KST\; results announced 14 August 2026\; program pe
 riod 20 August to 31 December 2026. Overseas participants (Track 2) must a
 ttend two in-person meetings in Jeonnam-Gwangju. HOW TO APPLY: submit the 
 application form and portfolio (PDF) by email to uartlabseoul@gmail.com. M
 ore info at urbanartlab.org/opencall. Free to apply.\n\nOrganisation: Gwan
 gju Media Art Platform (G.MAP)\nLocation: Jeonnam-Gwangju\, South Korea. I
 nternational applicants welcome (Track 2 only).\nAward: Track 2 (Interdisc
 iplinary Creation): creation and production grant up to KRW 30\,000\,000 p
 er team\, plus accommodation\, equipment\, studio space\, production and t
 ravel support\, exhibition on G.MAP spaces and large-scale public media pl
 atforms (LED Wall\, city media facades)\, and publication. Free to apply.\
 nDuration: Five-month creation support program\, August to December 2026\n
 \nMore: https://urbanartlab.org/opencall/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugran
 tdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://urbanartlab.org/opencall/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk
 &utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Jeonnam-Gwangju\, South Korea. International applicants welcome (T
 rack 2 only).
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:sixi-air-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260831T203817Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261115
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261116
SUMMARY:Deadline: Sixi International Artist-in-Residence Project 2027 (Nanj
 ing\, China)
DESCRIPTION:Launched in 2024 to support young emerging artists\, the Sixi I
 nternational Artist-in-Residence Project (run by Sixi Museum in Nanjing\, 
 China) facilitates exchanges between artists from different backgrounds an
 d helps them achieve creative breakthroughs and personal growth. The proje
 ct calls for artists across all disciplines and cultural backgrounds who a
 re ready to engage in dialogue with the city. TWO THEMES FOR 2027: 'Flux a
 nd Imprints: Contemporary Echoes of Migration History' and 'Folds of Text:
  Cross-Media Intertextuality and Intervention'. WHAT IS PROVIDED: living a
 nd working space (a city-centre apartment plus a loft studio in the outski
 rts to suit the research and production demands of different disciplines)\
 , financial support\, hardware facilities and staff assistance\, and help 
 establishing contacts with the local art scene\; by the end of the residen
 cy artists have the opportunity to showcase their outcomes in exhibitions.
  Nanjing combines traditional and contemporary Chinese culture\, and the p
 roject positions itself as one of the few local art residency programmes c
 ontributing to international cultural exchange in the city and to the dive
 rsified development of contemporary Chinese art. ELIGIBILITY: open to arti
 sts across all disciplines and cultural backgrounds. Deadline: 15 November
  2026. Apply via siximuseum.com.\n\nOrganisation: Sixi Museum\nLocation: N
 anjing\, China\nAward: Financial support plus living and working space: a 
 city-centre apartment and a loft studio in the outskirts\, hardware facili
 ties\, staff assistance\, and help connecting with the local art scene. No
  application fee.\nDuration: Residency period concludes with an exhibition
  of outcomes\n\nMore: https://siximuseum.com/en/residency/?utm_source=arti
 ficialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://siximuseum.com/en/residency/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantd
 esk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Nanjing\, China
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:fucina-futura-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260831T203817Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260820
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260821
SUMMARY:Deadline: Fucina Futura 2027 Residency (Marostica\, Italy)
DESCRIPTION:Fucina Futura is an artist residency in Marostica\, a small tow
 n about an hour from Venice\, offering a peaceful setting to develop resea
 rch in close contact with nature and the local community. The project span
 s two locations: the home designed by internationally renowned illustrator
  Elena Xausa near the historic centre\, and the atelier Fucina Ai Gorghi b
 y beloved local painter Daniele Marcon\, ideal for large-scale installatio
 ns. Led by visual artist Lavinia and curator Sofia (Futura Association)\, 
 the program invites residents to develop projects that engage with the com
 munity and the working location\, and encourages artists of any discipline
  to make full use of the large atelier. The central goal is the 'restituti
 on' to citizens\, fostering cultural exchange and community inclusion: thi
 s final phase is tailored to each artist and can take the form of an exhib
 ition\, performance\, workshop\, screening\, talk or informal sharing sess
 ion\, prioritising direct dialogue with the public and the contemporary re
 newal of local tradition. THREE residents are hosted together from 12 Apri
 l to 12 May 2027 and share a spacious house\; they receive a daily fee to 
 cover living expenses\, and travel expenses are also covered. Made possibl
 e by Culture Moves Europe. ELIGIBILITY: only artists residing in one of th
 e Creative Europe countries EXCEPT ITALY may apply. Creative Europe covers
  the 27 EU member states (other than Italy)\, plus Albania\, Armenia\, Bos
 nia and Herzegovina\, Georgia\, Iceland\, Kosovo\, Liechtenstein\, Moldova
 \, Montenegro\, North Macedonia\, Norway\, Serbia\, Tunisia and Ukraine\, 
 and includes the EU's Overseas Countries and Territories and Outermost Reg
 ions (Greenland\; French Guiana\, French Polynesia\, French Southern and A
 ntarctic Territories\, Guadeloupe\, Martinique\, Mayotte\, New Caledonia\,
  Reunion\, Saint Barthelemy\, Saint-Martin\, St. Pierre and Miquelon\, Wal
 lis and Futuna\; Azores\, Madeira\; Canary Islands\; Aruba\, Bonaire\, Cur
 acao\, Saba\, Sint Maarten\, Sint Eustatius). TIMELINE: apply via the Goog
 le Form by 20 August 2026\; selected artists informed by 30 August and mus
 t confirm participation by 8 September 2026.\n\nOrganisation: Futura Assoc
 iation (Fucina Futura)\, supported by Culture Moves Europe\nLocation: Maro
 stica\, Italy (one hour from Venice). Open to artists resident in a Creati
 ve Europe country except Italy.\nAward: Fully funded: daily fee to cover l
 iving expenses\, travel costs covered\, and shared house accommodation pro
 vided (supported by Culture Moves Europe). No application fee.\nDuration: 
 One month\, 12 April to 12 May 2027\; three residents hosted together\n\nM
 ore: https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLScwEmQ2EFrMoukgNorlOLE5kGvGr
 iMX0IdMBObmhfgRlSW-jQ/viewform?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_m
 edium=referral
URL:https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLScwEmQ2EFrMoukgNorlOLE5kGvGriM
 X0IdMBObmhfgRlSW-jQ/viewform?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_med
 ium=referral
LOCATION:Marostica\, Italy (one hour from Venice). Open to artists resident
  in a Creative Europe country except Italy.
END:VEVENT
