BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:instituto-sacatar-fellowship-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260831T203817Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260828
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260829
SUMMARY:Deadline: Instituto Sacatar: Sacatar Fellowship 2027 (Bahia\, Brazi
 l)
DESCRIPTION:Brazil's longest-running artist residency\, on the island of It
 aparica across the bay from Salvador\, hosting six to eight artists per se
 ssion for roughly eight weeks. Open to all creative disciplines and\, unus
 ually for this region\, to all nationalities\, which makes it one of the f
 ew genuinely international residencies in Latin America. Sacatar provides 
 full hosting (private room\, three meals daily\, individual studio\, laund
 ry\, local logistics and connections) but explicitly does NOT provide a st
 ipend\, airfare to Salvador\, art materials or discretionary local expense
 s\, so applicants must fund their own travel. Individual artists only\; gr
 oup proposals are not accepted and former Sacatar Fellows may not reapply.
  COVID vaccination is required. NOTE: there is a USD 25 application fee. A
 pply through SlideRoom by 28 August 2026. Contact info@sacatar.org.\n\nOrg
 anisation: Instituto Sacatar\nLocation: Itaparica island\, Bahia\, Brazil.
  Open to all nationalities.\nAward: Fully hosted residency: private bedroo
 m with attached bathroom\, three meals a day (except Saturday evenings\, S
 undays and Brazilian holidays)\, an individual studio suited to the discip
 line\, weekly laundry\, logistical support and airport transfer from Salva
 dor. NO STIPEND\, no airfare and no materials budget. USD 25 application f
 ee. One French artist may additionally receive airfare and a stipend throu
 gh Villa Fatumbi.\nDuration: Approximately eight weeks\; specific session 
 dates are listed in the application.\n\nMore: https://sacatar.org/en/fello
 wships/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://sacatar.org/en/fellowships/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantde
 sk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Itaparica island\, Bahia\, Brazil. Open to all nationalities.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:premio-klemm-artes-visuales-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260831T203817Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260904
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260905
SUMMARY:Deadline: Fundacion Klemm: 29th Premio Klemm a las Artes Visuales 2
 026
DESCRIPTION:The Premio Klemm is one of Argentina's longest-running visual a
 rts prizes\, now in its 29th edition\, awarded by the Fundacion Federico J
 orge Klemm in Buenos Aires. It is notable for a genuinely open definition 
 of medium: the entry categories explicitly include arte digital\, robotica
 \, video\, videoinstalacion\, audio and fotografia alongside painting\, dr
 awing and sculpture\, so technology-based practice is squarely in scope. E
 ntrants submit one work dated 2021 or later\, which must be durable rather
  than ephemeral. The top prizes are acquisition prizes\, so winning work e
 nters the foundation's collection. ELIGIBILITY IS RESTRICTED: Argentine na
 tionals (native or naturalised) or foreigners holding at least two years o
 f legal residence in Argentina\, aged 18 or over. Submissions close 4 Sept
 ember 2026 at 23:59. Prize amounts and the closing date are stated in the 
 bases y condiciones PDF linked from the entry site.\n\nOrganisation: Funda
 cion Federico Jorge Klemm\nLocation: Buenos Aires\, Argentina. Open to Arg
 entine nationals and to foreigners with at least two years of legal reside
 nce in Argentina.\nAward: First acquisition prize ARS 7\,000\,000 (around 
 USD 4\,800)\, second prize ARS 4\,000\,000 (around USD 2\,750). No entry f
 ee\; the foundation pays transport of selected works.\nDuration: Single pr
 ize with exhibition\; submitted work must be dated 2021 or later.\n\nMore:
  https://premioklemm.klemm.org.ar?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&ut
 m_medium=referral
URL:https://premioklemm.klemm.org.ar?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&
 utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Buenos Aires\, Argentina. Open to Argentine nationals and to forei
 gners with at least two years of legal residence in Argentina.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:gallery-1957-yaa-asantewaa-art-prize-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260831T203817Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260930
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261001
SUMMARY:Deadline: Gallery 1957: Yaa Asantewaa Art Prize 2026
DESCRIPTION:Annual prize from Gallery 1957 in Accra for women artists conne
 cted to Ghana and to Senegal\, which joins the prize for the first time in
  2026. Two winners are selected\, one from each country\, and each receive
 s USD 5\,000 in cash\, a three-month residency exchange in the partner cou
 ntry with flights\, artwork transport\, accommodation and materials covere
 d\, and a resulting exhibition with the gallery. ELIGIBILITY IS GEOGRAPHIC
 ALLY RESTRICTED: applicants must be female citizens of Ghana or Senegal\, 
 aged 18 or over\, living in Ghana\, Senegal or the diaspora\, and must pre
 sent a valid national ID or passport. Not open to international applicants
  without that citizenship. Apply by email to applications@gallery1957.com 
 with an artist bio or statement of no more than 200 words and a portfolio 
 of up to six high-resolution images or videos with captions\, both as PDFs
 . Questions go to awo@gallery1957.com. Deadline 30 September 2026.\n\nOrga
 nisation: Gallery 1957\nLocation: Accra\, Ghana and Saint-Louis / Dakar\, 
 Senegal. Open to female citizens of Ghana or Senegal residing in either co
 untry or in the diaspora.\nAward: USD 5\,000 cash per winner\, two winners
  (one Ghanaian\, one Senegalese)\, plus a fully covered three-month reside
 ncy exchange: flights\, transportation of artworks\, accommodation and mat
 erials. No application fee.\nDuration: Three-month residency exchange. The
  Ghanaian winner spends one month in Saint-Louis and two months in Dakar\;
  the Senegalese winner spends three months in Accra.\n\nMore: https://www.
 gallery1957.com/the-yaa-asantewaa-art-prize/?utm_source=artificialnouveaug
 rantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.gallery1957.com/the-yaa-asantewaa-art-prize/?utm_source=art
 ificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Accra\, Ghana and Saint-Louis / Dakar\, Senegal. Open to female ci
 tizens of Ghana or Senegal residing in either country or in the diaspora.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ace-pice-movilidad-2026-fase3@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260831T203817Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260907
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260908
SUMMARY:Deadline: Accion Cultural Espanola: PICE Movilidad 2026 (Phase 3)
DESCRIPTION:PICE Movilidad is AC/E's collaboration scheme with foreign cult
 ural institutions: a festival\, biennial\, museum\, venue\, gallery or pla
 tform OUTSIDE Spain applies for AC/E to cover the costs of programming Spa
 nish or Spain-resident artists\, collectives and cultural professionals in
  its own public programme. This is one of the clearest routes for a non-Sp
 anish festival to have a foreign national fund pay for part of its program
 me. Ten thematic areas are covered including Artes visuales\, Musica y cre
 acion sonora\, Podcast\, Videojuego y animacion and Arquitectura y diseno\
 , so tech-crossover\, sound-art and media-art programming is squarely in s
 cope. For visual arts and architecture/design\, covered costs include prod
 uction materials\, purchase or rental of technical equipment\, hiring of t
 echnicians\, curators\, coordinators and designers\, reproduction and exhi
 bition rights\, logistics and transport of works\, publications\, document
 ation\, accommodation\, per diems\, travel and insurance\; for Musica y cr
 eacion sonora coverage is narrower (travel\, accommodation\, per diems\, i
 nternal transport). Non-EU and UK organisations are fully eligible\; there
  is no EU-membership requirement. Natural persons are barred. TIMING: Phas
 e 3 closes 7 September 2026\, provisional list 21 October\, definitive awa
 rd list 30 October\, and Phase 3 projects may not begin before 1 November 
 2026\, so this window cannot retro-fund an event already scheduled for aut
 umn 2026.\n\nOrganisation: Accion Cultural Espanola (AC/E)\nLocation: Anyw
 here outside Spain\, at the applicant's own venue or event. Applicant must
  be a foreign entity constituted outside Spain.\nAward: Max EUR 15\,000 pe
 r applicant per call\, per event and per thematic area\; within that\, max
  EUR 5\,000 per participant or collective. Total 2026 call budget EUR 1\,8
 10\,000 (Musica y creacion sonora EUR 320\,000\, Artes visuales EUR 200\,0
 00\, Videojuego y animacion EUR 90\,000\, Arquitectura y diseno EUR 90\,00
 0\, Podcast EUR 90\,000). Mandatory co-financing: the applicant must commi
 t at least 50 percent of each proposal's total budget. No application fee.
 \nDuration: Single event or project\; Phase 3 activities must start on or 
 after 1 November 2026 and finish before 28 February 2027.\n\nMore: https:/
 /www.accioncultural.es/es/movilidad-2026?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrant
 desk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.accioncultural.es/es/movilidad-2026?utm_source=artificialno
 uveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Anywhere outside Spain\, at the applicant's own venue or event. Ap
 plicant must be a foreign entity constituted outside Spain.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ace-pice-visitantes-2026-fase3@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260831T203817Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260907
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260908
SUMMARY:Deadline: Accion Cultural Espanola: PICE Visitantes 2026 (Phase 3)
DESCRIPTION:PICE Visitantes is the inbound mirror of PICE Movilidad: a Span
 ish festival\, biennial\, fair\, museum or platform applies for AC/E to fu
 nd bringing international programmers\, curators\, producers and cultural 
 professionals to its event in Spain\, so that they meet Spanish artists an
 d go on to programme them abroad. It is direct money to an organisation to
  enrich a festival or public programme it is already hosting. The same ten
  thematic areas apply as in Movilidad\, including Artes visuales\, Musica 
 y creacion sonora\, Podcast and Videojuego y animacion\, giving good cover
 age for media-arts\, sound-art and creative-technology events. Covered cos
 ts are travel\, accommodation\, travel insurance\, internal transport\, te
 xt translation and simultaneous or consecutive interpretation for the invi
 ted visitors\, with the exact list varying slightly by thematic area. Only
  entities constituted in Spain may apply\; natural persons are barred. Inv
 ited guests may come from any country including non-EU and the UK. TIMING:
  Phase 3 closes 7 September 2026\, provisional list 21 October\, definitiv
 e list 30 October\, and visits may not start before 1 November 2026. Appli
 cations go through the AC/E PICE online system in Spanish or English with 
 no fee.\n\nOrganisation: Accion Cultural Espanola (AC/E)\nLocation: Spain.
  The host event must take place in Spain and the applicant must be constit
 uted in Spain.\nAward: Max EUR 20\,000 per applicant per call\, per event 
 and per thematic area\; within that\, max EUR 2\,000 per international vis
 itor. Total 2026 call budget EUR 1\,200\,000 (Cine EUR 180\,000\, Artes vi
 suales EUR 160\,000\, Musica y creacion sonora EUR 150\,000\, Literatura E
 UR 150\,000\, Arquitectura y diseno EUR 90\,000\, Podcast EUR 90\,000\, Vi
 deojuego y animacion EUR 90\,000). No application fee.\nDuration: Single e
 vent\; Phase 3 visits must start on or after 1 November 2026 and finish be
 fore 28 February 2027.\n\nMore: https://www.accioncultural.es/es/visitante
 s-2026?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.accioncultural.es/es/visitantes-2026?utm_source=artificialn
 ouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Spain. The host event must take place in Spain and the applicant m
 ust be constituted in Spain.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:fondazione-crt-orizzonti-live-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260831T203817Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260915
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260916
SUMMARY:Deadline: Fondazione CRT: Orizzonti L.I.V.E. 2026 (second session)
DESCRIPTION:Orizzonti L.I.V.E. is Fondazione CRT's flagship thematic call f
 or organisations that programme live performance as a driver of territoria
 l transformation. The acronym stands for Luoghi\, Impatto\, Visioni\, Ener
 gia\, and stated priorities are strengthening organisations rooted in thei
 r territory\, audience development reaching new publics\, social inclusion
  and access for economically or socially fragile audiences\, professional 
 engagement of young musicians\, actors and dancers\, audience engagement a
 imed at under-25s\, stable networks and strategic partnerships\, and envir
 onmental sustainability aligned with Agenda 2030. This is festival and sea
 son funding at meaningful scale: the maximum request is EUR 100\,000 and t
 he overall project budget must itself be at least EUR 100\,000\, with co-f
 inancing covering at least 70 percent of eligible costs\, so the applicant
  must bring roughly EUR 70\,000 from other sources. The 2026 call runs in 
 two sessions: the first closed 27 February 2026\, and the second closes 15
  September 2026 at 15:00 Italian time. Applications go through rol.fondazi
 onecrt.it. SCOPE CAVEAT: this is broad live-performance funding rather tha
 n a media-arts line\, so it fits experimental performance\, sound art and 
 hybrid live work but also covers conventional music and theatre. Non-EU an
 d UK organisations can realistically only participate as project partners\
 , not as lead applicants.\n\nOrganisation: Fondazione CRT (Fondazione Cass
 a di Risparmio di Torino)\nLocation: Piedmont and Valle d'Aosta\, Italy. A
 ctivities must be delivered in those regions\; the applicant does not itse
 lf have to be headquartered there.\nAward: Max EUR 100\,000 requestable. T
 he project's own budget must be at least EUR 100\,000. Mandatory co-financ
 ing of at least 70 percent of eligible project costs\, so CRT covers a max
 imum of 30 percent. The requested amount is assessed against the applicant
 's last approved annual accounts and grant history. No application fee.\nD
 uration: Project period set in the application\; extensions of the grant-u
 se deadline of up to 12 months may be requested.\n\nMore: https://www.fond
 azionecrt.it/bandi-progetti/orizzonti-l-i-v-e/?utm_source=artificialnouvea
 ugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.fondazionecrt.it/bandi-progetti/orizzonti-l-i-v-e/?utm_sour
 ce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Piedmont and Valle d'Aosta\, Italy. Activities must be delivered i
 n those regions\; the applicant does not itself have to be headquartered t
 here.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:kulturdirektoratet-tverrfaglig-kulturvirksomhet-2026@artificialnouveau.
 github.io
DTSTAMP:20260831T203817Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260915
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260916
SUMMARY:Deadline: Kulturdirektoratet: Cross-Disciplinary Cultural Activity\
 , Events\, Organisers and Venues (2026 autumn round)
DESCRIPTION:Kulturdirektoratet's main scheme for multi-artistic and cross-d
 isciplinary events\, organisers and venues\, and the natural Norwegian rou
 te for a festival or biennial that does not sit inside a single artform co
 mmittee. It funds single events\, event series\, festivals and seminars wi
 th cross-disciplinary relevance\, plus year-round operation of organisatio
 ns with a multi-artistic profile\, which covers media arts\, digital cultu
 re and experimental sound programming presented alongside other forms. Art
  production itself\, closed workshops\, infrastructure investment and acti
 vity already completed before the deadline are not funded. Two application
  rounds run in 2026: 8 April 2026 (project grants\, closed) and 15 Septemb
 er 2026 at 13:00 (project grants plus activity grants for the 2027 operati
 ng year). Project grants accept individuals\, private and public instituti
 ons\, and organisations\, while activity grants require an organisation nu
 mber or a named\, separately budgeted activity within a larger entity\, ex
 isting for at least one year and not already receiving permanent annual st
 ate funding. The scheme never fully finances a project\, so a credible co-
 financing plan is expected. FLAG: decision dates and foreign-applicant eli
 gibility are not published on the scheme page\; award notifications arrive
  via the application portal.\n\nOrganisation: Kulturdirektoratet (Arts and
  Culture Norway)\nLocation: Norway. Activity is expected to take place in 
 Norway\, though international artists and partners can be programmed.\nAwa
 rd: NOK. No fixed minimum or maximum published\; grant sizes are assessed 
 against the project budget\, financing plan and available funds. Kulturdir
 ektoratet states it does not provide full financing\, so co-financing is r
 equired in practice but no fixed percentage is set. Historical award level
 s are published in the scheme's public decision database. No application f
 ee.\nDuration: Project grants for single events or series\; activity grant
 s cover the 2027 operating year.\n\nMore: https://www.kulturdirektoratet.n
 o/tilskuddsordninger/tverrfaglig-kulturvirksomhet-arrangementer-arrangoere
 r-og-arenaer?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.kulturdirektoratet.no/tilskuddsordninger/tverrfaglig-kultur
 virksomhet-arrangementer-arrangoerer-og-arenaer?utm_source=artificialnouve
 augrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Norway. Activity is expected to take place in Norway\, though inte
 rnational artists and partners can be programmed.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:kulturdirektoratet-arrangoerstoette-visuell-kunst-2026@artificialnouvea
 u.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260831T203817Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260915
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260916
SUMMARY:Deadline: Kulturdirektoratet: Arrangorstotte Visuell Kunst\, Visual
  Art Organisers Support (2026 round)
DESCRIPTION:This scheme gives operating and programme support to visual art
  organisers in Norway\, covering exhibition and event programming\, conten
 t production\, salaries\, artist fees\, venue costs including rent\, utili
 ties and internet\, and administrative expenses. Because it funds the orga
 niser rather than a single artwork\, it is the relevant route for an artis
 t-run space\, biennial organisation or media-arts venue running a recurrin
 g public programme. Applicants must demonstrate artistic and cultural expe
 rtise\, innovation and distinctiveness. Eligibility is limited to bodies w
 ith their own registration number\, or a separately named and budgeted act
 ivity within a larger organisation\, existing for at least one year prior 
 to application\, and organisations already receiving permanent annual stat
 e funding are excluded. The 2026 application deadline is 15 September 2026
  at 13:00. Kulturdirektoratet explicitly warns that applicants often recei
 ve less than requested or are rejected despite quality proposals\, so co-f
 inancing is necessary. FLAG: amounts\, decision lag and foreign-applicant 
 eligibility are not published on the funder's page\; results arrive throug
 h the application portal with an acceptance deadline in the decision lette
 r.\n\nOrganisation: Kulturdirektoratet (Arts and Culture Norway)\nLocation
 : Norway. Foreign applicant eligibility is not stated on the scheme page.\
 nAward: NOK. No published minimum or maximum\; award sizes vary with budge
 t and available funds and previous awards are listed in the scheme's decis
 ion database. Kulturdirektoratet does not provide full financing\, so co-f
 inancing is expected and applicants often receive less than requested. No 
 application fee.\nDuration: Operating and programme support\, typically co
 vering the following activity year.\n\nMore: https://www.kulturdirektorate
 t.no/tilskuddsordninger/arrangoerstoette-visuell-kunst?utm_source=artifici
 alnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.kulturdirektoratet.no/tilskuddsordninger/arrangoerstoette-v
 isuell-kunst?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Norway. Foreign applicant eligibility is not stated on the scheme 
 page.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:statens-kunstfond-production-exhibitions-2026@artificialnouveau.github.
 io
DTSTAMP:20260831T203817Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260924
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260925
SUMMARY:Deadline: Statens Kunstfond: Production and Exhibitions\, Contempor
 ary Art in Denmark and Abroad (2026 autumn round)
DESCRIPTION:The Danish Arts Foundation's Production and Exhibitions program
 me funds the production\, dissemination and exhibition of contemporary art
  in Denmark and abroad\, and it is one of the few Nordic national schemes 
 a foreign organisation can apply to directly. Eligible costs include creat
 ing new works where an exhibition agreement is in place\, exhibition costs
 \, exhibition programming featuring Danish or international artists\, prom
 otion tied to an exhibition\, and honorariums covering artists' work and i
 nstallation time\, which lets a festival or biennial cover commission and 
 artist-fee lines. THE KEY CONDITION for non-Danish applicants is that the 
 exhibition must feature Danish artists\; Danish artists and venues face no
  such restriction. No minimum or maximum grant is published since the comm
 ittee decides case by case\, and previous award levels are visible on the 
 site. Two 2026 deadlines apply: 26 March 2026 (closed) and 24 September 20
 26 at 14:00\, with the application form opening one month before each dead
 line. TIMING: applicants receive a response no later than twelve weeks aft
 er the deadline\, so expect a decision by mid-December 2026. Applications 
 must go through the Danish digital subsidy portal\; submissions outside it
  are rejected except in very special circumstances. FLAG: earliest-start-d
 ate rules are not specified on the funder's page.\n\nOrganisation: Statens
  Kunstfond (Danish Arts Foundation)\nLocation: Denmark and abroad. Non-Dan
 ish venues and organisations may apply\, but only for exhibitions that fea
 ture Danish artists.\nAward: DKK. No published minimum or maximum\; the co
 mmittee assesses each application on its merits and historical awards are 
 published on the site. No stated co-financing requirement. No application 
 fee. Applications must be submitted digitally via the Danish subsidy porta
 l (Tilskudsportalen).\nDuration: Project-length\; production and exhibitio
 n periods vary.\n\nMore: https://www.kunst.dk/english/funding-programmes/e
 xhibition-of-danish-art-abroad?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_m
 edium=referral
URL:https://www.kunst.dk/english/funding-programmes/exhibition-of-danish-ar
 t-abroad?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Denmark and abroad. Non-Danish venues and organisations may apply\
 , but only for exhibitions that feature Danish artists.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:fonds-daku-global-village-kids-digital-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260831T203817Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261001
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261002
SUMMARY:Deadline: Fonds Darstellende Kuenste: GLOBAL VILLAGE KIDS im digita
 len Raum (2026 round)
DESCRIPTION:The digital-space strand of the Fonds Darstellende Kuenste GLOB
 AL VILLAGE KIDS programme\, funding format-open and results-open artistic 
 projects and artist-participatory approaches in digital and hybrid perform
 ing arts. Eligible artistic fields explicitly include digital performing a
 rts alongside performance\, theatre\, dance\, musical theatre\, puppet the
 atre and contemporary circus\, which makes it usable for hybrid or online 
 public programmes. The applicant must be a coalition of at least three leg
 ally constituted organisations spanning arts and culture\, education and c
 ivil society\, all German-based\, so this is genuinely institution-facing 
 rather than artist-facing\; individual artists cannot apply\, and schools 
 and kindergartens may participate as partners but cannot be the applying o
 rganisation. Two tiers exist: laboratory projects at EUR 5\,000 to 15\,000
  requiring a minimum 30 hours of work\, and process projects at EUR 15\,00
 0 to 40\,000 requiring a minimum 60 hours\, both inclusive of a 7 percent 
 administrative fee. FULL FINANCING is available with no matching requireme
 nt\, which is unusual and valuable. TIMING: the deadline is 1 October 2026
  with the earliest permitted project start on 1 January 2027\, so the deci
 sion lag is roughly three months. Applications go exclusively through the 
 kumasta online database. FIT CAVEAT: the programme targets children and yo
 ung people aged 3 to 18 in situations of social\, financial or educational
  disadvantage\, so it suits a digital-arts programme with a youth particip
 ation core rather than a general public festival.\n\nOrganisation: Fonds D
 arstellende Kuenste e.V.\nLocation: Germany. All coalition members must be
  based in Germany\, though non-German artists may be involved as contracte
 d artists.\nAward: Laboratory projects EUR 5\,000 to 15\,000\; process pro
 jects EUR 15\,000 to 40\,000. Both figures include a 7 percent administrat
 ive overhead. Full financing model\, no co-financing required. No applicat
 ion fee.\nDuration: Earliest start 1 January 2027\; projects must conclude
  by 31 August 2027\; final reports due 30 September 2027.\n\nMore: https:/
 /www.fonds-daku.de/foerderung/foerderprogramme/global-village-kids-2/globa
 l-village-kids-im-digitalen-raum/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&ut
 m_medium=referral
URL:https://www.fonds-daku.de/foerderung/foerderprogramme/global-village-ki
 ds-2/global-village-kids-im-digitalen-raum/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugr
 antdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Germany. All coalition members must be based in Germany\, though n
 on-German artists may be involved as contracted artists.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:fondazione-crt-ordinarie-arte-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260831T203817Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261015
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261016
SUMMARY:Deadline: Fondazione CRT: Bando Ordinarie 2026\, Arte\, attivita e 
 beni culturali\, Progetti (second session)
DESCRIPTION:The Bando Ordinarie is Fondazione CRT's open\, non-thematic rou
 te: organisations can request support for initiatives that fit the foundat
 ion's statutory aims but do not fall under any of its thematic calls\, acr
 oss three areas of which one is Arte\, attivita e beni culturali (branded 
 Meraviglia). It is the right door for public programmes\, cultural project
 s\, media and digital-culture initiatives and events that are not live per
 formance\, exhibitions\, film festivals or restoration. READ THE EXCLUSION
  LIST CAREFULLY: live performance goes to NoteSipari or Orizzonti L.I.V.E.
 \, exhibition-format initiatives and film festivals go to Immagini e Prosp
 ettive\, heritage restoration goes to BeST\, and accessible territorial-sh
 owcase events go to Eventi for All\, so Ordinarie is the residual arts rou
 te. Non-profit entities and institutions operating in the reference territ
 ory are eligible\, and because the applicant does not need to be headquart
 ered in Piedmont or Valle d'Aosta this is genuinely open to organisations 
 based elsewhere\, including non-EU and UK\, that run a programme in those 
 regions. The project route has two deadlines: the first was 30 April 2026 
 and the second session is open 1 July to 15 October 2026 at 15:00 Italian 
 time. Organisations receiving an activity-support grant cannot also benefi
 t from other CRT calls in the same calendar year. Applications are made th
 rough rol.fondazionecrt.it.\n\nOrganisation: Fondazione CRT (Fondazione Ca
 ssa di Risparmio di Torino)\nLocation: Piedmont and Valle d'Aosta\, Italy.
  The project must be delivered in those regions\, but the applicant does n
 ot need to be headquartered there.\nAward: No published fixed minimum or m
 aximum for the arts strand\; grant size is set case by case against the pr
 oject budget and the applicant's financial capacity. Co-financing is not u
 niversally mandated but specific categories carry thresholds (conference a
 nd seminar requests above EUR 10\,000 are inadmissible without co-financin
 g of at least two thirds of budgeted spend). Across all three areas Fondaz
 ione CRT distributed roughly EUR 5.5 million to 349 projects in a single r
 ecent Ordinarie session. No application fee.\nDuration: Project-based\; gr
 ant-use period governed by the Regolamento Generale di Erogazione 2026\, w
 ith extensions of up to 12 months available on request.\n\nMore: https://w
 ww.fondazionecrt.it/bandi-progetti/arte-cultura-ordinarie/?utm_source=arti
 ficialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.fondazionecrt.it/bandi-progetti/arte-cultura-ordinarie/?utm
 _source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Piedmont and Valle d'Aosta\, Italy. The project must be delivered 
 in those regions\, but the applicant does not need to be headquartered the
 re.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:perform-europe-third-open-call-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260831T203817Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261022
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261023
SUMMARY:Deadline: Perform Europe: Third Open Call for Cross-Border Touring 
 (2026-28 edition)
DESCRIPTION:Perform Europe is the EU's dedicated cross-border touring schem
 e for the performing arts\, run by a six-organisation consortium and co-fu
 nded by Creative Europe. It funds partnerships of at least three organisat
 ions from three different Creative Europe countries to tour a finished per
 forming arts work in at least three countries\, with an explicit emphasis 
 on greener\, more inclusive and more equitable touring practice. Eligible 
 disciplines are circus\, dance\, outdoor arts\, performance art\, puppetry
  and theatre\; LIVE MUSIC AND OPERA ARE EXCLUDED\, and production costs fo
 r new creations are not covered since the work must already be finished be
 fore 1 March 2027. Applicants pick one of three grant tiers with no fixed 
 criteria per tier\, and may request up to EUR 5\,000 in top-ups for access
 ibility and sustainability measures. Five percent of the total fund is rin
 g-fenced for proposals involving Ukrainian partners or supporting the Ukra
 inian performing arts sector. All 41 Creative Europe countries are eligibl
 e\, including Albania\, Armenia\, Bosnia and Herzegovina\, Georgia\, Icela
 nd\, Kosovo\, Liechtenstein\, Moldova\, Montenegro\, North Macedonia\, Nor
 way\, Serbia\, Tunisia and Ukraine\, but the UK is not. TIMING: applicatio
 ns close 22 October 2026 at 23:59 CEST\, selected partnerships are announc
 ed in January 2027\, and activity may only start from 1 March 2027. A Matc
 hmaking Platform with over 2\,300 registered professionals is available fo
 r finding partners before applying. CORE PRIORITY: each partnership must p
 ick either diversity and inclusion or the fight against climate change as 
 its core priority\, and must also include measures addressing the other on
 e\; that choice has to run visibly through the whole application rather th
 an sit in one section. WHO COUNTS AS A PARTNER: both organisations and ind
 ividual professionals are eligible\, so a partner can be an artist\, colle
 ctive\, company\, producer\, presenter\, venue\, festival\, residency\, ed
 ucational institution or NGO. Eligibility is decided by where you are lega
 lly based. The partnership appoints a lead partner who submits\, signs and
  receives the grant. ELIGIBLE COSTS: artistic fees and salaries\, travel\,
  accommodation\, subsistence\, administration\, reporting\, communication\
 , translation\, surtitling\, equipment transport\, copyright fees\, access
  and environmental measures\, complementary activities and capacity buildi
 ng. Venue and equipment rental or purchase is capped at 5 percent of the r
 equested grant\, and preparation costs for presenting an existing work at 
 10 percent. PAYMENT: 60 percent after signing\, 20 percent after the first
  narrative and financial report is approved\, and the final 20 percent aft
 er completion and EU approval of Perform Europe's own final report. Top-up
 s are reimbursed only after the project ends and documentation is approved
 \, so budget for the cash-flow gap. PRACTICAL: every partner must register
  for a Perform Europe account before submission and approval can take seve
 ral working days\, so do not leave that to the last week.\n\nOrganisation:
  Perform Europe (IETM\, EFA\, Circostrada\, European Dancehouse Network\, 
 Pearle*\, IDEA Consult)\, co-funded by Creative Europe\nLocation: Europe-w
 ide\; touring must happen in at least 3 Creative Europe countries. The UK 
 is NOT eligible.\nAward: Three grant tiers of EUR 15\,000\, EUR 25\,000 or
  EUR 55\,000\, plus top-ups of up to EUR 5\,000\, giving a EUR 60\,000 cei
 ling per partnership. EUR 1.4 million total across at least 25 partnership
 s\, covering up to 100 percent of eligible costs\, so no matching funds ar
 e needed. TOP-UP RATES: green mobility EUR 400 per person per presentation
  date\; accessibility support EUR 400 per person per presentation date\; f
 amily top-up EUR 200 per child per presentation date\; audience access EUR
  800 per presentation date\; visa EUR 120 per person needing one\; oversea
 s and outermost regions EUR 175 per person per presentation date. No appli
 cation fee.\nDuration: Touring and implementation 1 March 2027 to 31 Janua
 ry 2028 (11 months).\n\nMore: https://performeurope.eu/open-call/?utm_sour
 ce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://performeurope.eu/open-call/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantde
 sk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Europe-wide\; touring must happen in at least 3 Creative Europe co
 untries. The UK is NOT eligible.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:gemeente-rotterdam-projectsubsidie-cultuur-2026@artificialnouveau.githu
 b.io
DTSTAMP:20260831T203817Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260901
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260902
SUMMARY:Deadline: Gemeente Rotterdam: Project Subsidy Culture (Projectsubsi
 die Cultuur\, September 2026 round)
DESCRIPTION:Rotterdam's standing project fund for one-off artistic and cult
 ural activity\, and the most accessible municipal route for festivals\, ex
 hibitions and public programmes in the city. The discipline list names e-c
 ulture outright alongside moving image and artistic film\, design and fash
 ion\, visual arts and photography\, architecture\, spoken word and all hyb
 rid forms\, so media-art and creative-technology programming is squarely i
 n scope. Both non-profit legal entities and natural persons may apply\, so
  individual artists are eligible. There is no published maximum per applic
 ation\; the real constraint is the EUR 272\,000 available per round agains
 t roughly 130 competing applications. Six rounds run every year with fixed
  closing dates on the first of January\, March\, May\, July\, September an
 d November. TIMING RULE: the activity may not start until eight weeks afte
 r the closing date of the round applied in\, so a 1 September 2026 applica
 tion supports activity from late October 2026 onward. Decisions normally a
 rrive within eight weeks of the round deadline\, extendable to 20 weeks. A
 ssociations and foundations apply via eHerkenning\, individuals via DigiD.
  Organisations already receiving Rotterdamse Culturele Basis\, Cultuurplan
 \, Impulsregeling\, national BIS\, Lokale Culturele Programmering or a CBK
  Rotterdam practice contribution are excluded.\n\nOrganisation: Gemeente R
 otterdam (Municipality of Rotterdam)\nLocation: Activity must serve a Rott
 erdam interest and take place in or for Rotterdam. City-restricted by rele
 vance of the activity rather than by applicant address.\nAward: No stated 
 per-application cap. Annual pot EUR 1\,632\,000 split into six rounds of E
 UR 272\,000\, with roughly 130 applications per round. Discipline sub-caps
 : book writing max EUR 4\,500\; moving image R&D max EUR 4\,000\; moving-i
 mage production max EUR 12\,500\; post-production max EUR 4\,000. Applican
 ts must demonstrably seek other funds or sponsors. Awards over EUR 50\,000
  require an auditor's statement at reporting\, at the applicant's cost. No
  application fee.\nDuration: Single one-off project.\n\nMore: https://www.
 rotterdam.nl/projectsubsidie-cultuur-aanvragen?utm_source=artificialnouvea
 ugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.rotterdam.nl/projectsubsidie-cultuur-aanvragen?utm_source=a
 rtificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Activity must serve a Rotterdam interest and take place in or for 
 Rotterdam. City-restricted by relevance of the activity rather than by app
 licant address.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:kunstraad-groningen-tweejarige-programmaregeling-2027@artificialnouveau
 .github.io
DTSTAMP:20260831T203817Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260901
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260902
SUMMARY:Deadline: Kunstraad Groningen: Two-Year Programme Scheme (Tweejarig
 e Programmaregeling\, 2027-2028)
DESCRIPTION:This is the Groningen scheme that actually funds festivals\, an
 d the correct counterpart to the Kunstraad's Projectenregeling\, which exp
 licitly excludes festivals and recurring programmes and redirects them her
 e. It supports coherent\, continuous public activity across 2027 and 2028 
 in all arts and heritage disciplines\, naming recurring production series\
 , festivals and programme lines as eligible\, with no exclusion of media a
 rt\, digital culture or experimental sound work. Annually recurring festiv
 als with a year-round paid organisation are explicitly named as eligible a
 pplicants. Awards run from EUR 5\,000 to 40\,000 per year against an annua
 l pot of EUR 325\,000\, capped at one third of total project costs\, so tw
 o thirds must come from municipal funds\, national funds\, box office or o
 wn contribution. Unusually\, the money may also be used to strengthen the 
 organisation itself on the business side\, not only to pay for programme c
 ontent. The application window is 1 July to 1 September 2026\, closing at 
 23:59\, and only applications received on time are processed. Applications
  must be submitted in Dutch via the Mijn Kunstraad portal with fair-pay st
 andards applied in the budget. Funding covers nothing before 1 January 202
 7. Professional non-profit organisations only\; amateur associations and i
 ndividual artists are directed elsewhere. Material investments\, equipment
  purchases and housing costs are excluded.\n\nOrganisation: Kunstraad Gron
 ingen\, on behalf of the municipality and province of Groningen\nLocation:
  Municipality and province of Groningen. The applicant organisation must b
 e based and active in Groningen. Region-restricted.\nAward: EUR 5\,000 min
 imum to EUR 40\,000 maximum per year across two years\, so up to EUR 80\,0
 00 total. Covers a maximum of one third of total project costs\, requiring
  roughly 67 percent co-financing. Annual scheme budget EUR 325\,000. No ap
 plication fee.\nDuration: Two years of programming\, covering 2027 and 202
 8.\n\nMore: https://kunstraadgroningen.nl/subsidies/tweejarige-programmare
 geling/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://kunstraadgroningen.nl/subsidies/tweejarige-programmaregeling/?u
 tm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Municipality and province of Groningen. The applicant organisation
  must be based and active in Groningen. Region-restricted.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:fondspodiumkunsten-buitenlandse-voorstellingen-2026@artificialnouveau.g
 ithub.io
DTSTAMP:20260831T203817Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260923
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260924
SUMMARY:Deadline: Fonds Podiumkunsten: Foreign Performances or Concerts in 
 the Netherlands (round 4\, 2026)
DESCRIPTION:Fonds Podiumkunsten's route for Dutch festivals and venues brin
 ging in exceptional foreign performing arts and concerts that Dutch audien
 ces would otherwise not see. The applicant must be a Netherlands-registere
 d legal entity running a venue or festival and carrying artistic and finan
 cial responsibility for its own programme\, so individuals and sole trader
 s cannot apply. Grants are calculated from travel and transport costs of t
 he incoming artists\, at a maximum of EUR 25\,000 per production and EUR 7
 5\,000 per applicant across several productions. The core test is that the
  foreign work is rarely or never seen in the Netherlands and substantially
  enriches the existing Dutch offer\, which favours experimental\, non-cano
 nical and cross-disciplinary programming over mainstream touring. Experime
 ntal music and sound-art programming is not excluded\; the selection crite
 rion is rarity and added value\, not genre. Applications go through the Mi
 jn Fonds portal and there is no fee. Four rounds run each year. TIMING: be
 cause the scheme competes against a shared EUR 267\,500 per-round pot and 
 assessment takes several weeks after the deadline\, organisers should appl
 y at least one full round ahead of the performance date and must not have 
 the activity already underway. Success rate in 2025 was 60 percent of 33 a
 pplications.\n\nOrganisation: Fonds Podiumkunsten (Performing Arts Fund NL
 )\nLocation: Activity must take place in the Netherlands. Applicants from 
 Aruba\, Bonaire\, Curacao\, Sint Maarten\, Saba and Sint Eustatius are als
 o in scope. No city or region restriction.\nAward: Maximum EUR 25\,000 per
  production\, capped at EUR 75\,000 for an applicant presenting multiple p
 roductions. Calculated on travel and transport costs of the foreign artist
 s and their production only. EUR 267\,500 available per round shared acros
 s this scheme and two sibling internationalisation schemes. Fees\, venue a
 nd production costs stay with the applicant. No application fee.\nDuration
 : Single performances or a short run of concerts within one programme or f
 estival edition.\n\nMore: https://fondspodiumkunsten.nl/subsidies/buitenla
 ndse-voorstellingen-of-concerten-in-nederland?utm_source=artificialnouveau
 grantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://fondspodiumkunsten.nl/subsidies/buitenlandse-voorstellingen-of-
 concerten-in-nederland?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=re
 ferral
LOCATION:Activity must take place in the Netherlands. Applicants from Aruba
 \, Bonaire\, Curacao\, Sint Maarten\, Saba and Sint Eustatius are also in 
 scope. No city or region restriction.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:gemeente-utrecht-projectsubsidie-cultuur-2026@artificialnouveau.github.
 io
DTSTAMP:20260831T203817Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260925
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260926
SUMMARY:Deadline: Gemeente Utrecht: Project Subsidy Culture (Projectsubsidi
 e Cultuur\, round 3 2026)
DESCRIPTION:Utrecht's main project fund for cultural activity with a public
  presentation in the city\, covering all art forms including experimental 
 and cross-disciplinary work. Individuals\, foundations\, associations and 
 companies are all eligible. Two bands apply: Category A of EUR 1\,000 to 5
 \,000 assessed on artistic importance and entrepreneurship\, and Category 
 B of EUR 5\,000 to 20\,000 which adds meaning for the city as a third crit
 erion. The activity must be exceptional or innovative\, or otherwise of va
 lue to the city\, its residents or the Utrecht cultural sector\; professio
 nal projects and amateur\, education or participation projects both qualif
 y. Three rounds run each year and the next closes 25 September 2026 at 17:
 00 CET. TIMING RULE\, which catches applicants out: for professional arts 
 applications the presentation may not take place earlier than 13 weeks aft
 er the round's closing date\, and for participatory applications the proje
 ct may not start earlier than 13 weeks after that date\, so a 25 September
  2026 application supports activity from late December 2026 onward. Decisi
 ons are issued no later than 13 weeks after the closing date\, following r
 eview by an independent Adviescommissie Projectsubsidies. Documentation is
  capped at 15 pages\, or 5 pages if a video is included. Applications go t
 hrough mijnsubsidie.utrecht.nl with DigiD or eHerkenning. Utrecht also run
 s a rolling Impulssubsidie Cultuur of up to EUR 2\,500 for first-time appl
 icants only\, open through 31 December 2026.\n\nOrganisation: Gemeente Utr
 echt (Municipality of Utrecht)\nLocation: Activity must have a presentatio
 n moment in Utrecht and benefit residents of the municipality of Utrecht. 
 City-restricted by presentation location\, not by applicant residence.\nAw
 ard: Category A: EUR 1\,000 to 5\,000. Category B: EUR 5\,000 to 20\,000. 
 No fixed co-financing percentage\, but a budget and coverage plan is manda
 tory. eHerkenning purchase costs may be included in the budget and are rei
 mbursed if awarded. No application fee.\nDuration: Single project.\n\nMore
 : https://loket.digitaal.utrecht.nl/nl/producten/projectsubsidie-cultuur-a
 anvragen?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://loket.digitaal.utrecht.nl/nl/producten/projectsubsidie-cultuur-
 aanvragen?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Activity must have a presentation moment in Utrecht and benefit re
 sidents of the municipality of Utrecht. City-restricted by presentation lo
 cation\, not by applicant residence.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:bng-cultuurfonds-projectsubsidies-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260831T203817Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260927
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260928
SUMMARY:Deadline: BNG Cultuurfonds: Project Grants (round closing September
  2026)
DESCRIPTION:BNG Cultuurfonds funds arts and culture projects that add value
  for Dutch municipalities and their inhabitants\, explicitly including tem
 porary exhibitions\, public programmes and festivals developed by professi
 onal makers. Media art\, digital culture and cross-disciplinary work quali
 fy as long as a professional maker's artistic vision leads the project. On
 ly stichtingen (foundations) may apply: no sole traders\, associations\, i
 ndividuals\, or foundations in formation. Applications go by email to aanv
 raag.cultuurfonds@bngbank.nl with a signed form\, a project plan of at mos
 t 3\,500 words\, a specified budget and coverage plan\, current statutes a
 nd a recent KvK extract. The grant is EUR 5\,000 to 15\,000 and can cover 
 no more than 35 percent of the budget. TIMING IS THE MAIN TRAP: for the 27
  September 2026 deadline\, feedback comes at the end of December 2026 and 
 the project may not start before 1 January 2027\, with applications for ea
 rlier-starting projects rejected outright with no exceptions. Missing docu
 ments are flagged up to one week before the deadline\, so anything submitt
 ed in the final week cannot be corrected. Plan for roughly four months of 
 lead time. Excluded: amateur art\, talent development\, education-focused 
 projects\, semi-permanent public art\, publications\, building or renovati
 on\, and regular operating costs. Further rounds: 3 January 2027\, 28 Marc
 h 2027\, 27 June 2027\, 3 October 2027 and 2 January 2028.\n\nOrganisation
 : Stichting BNG Cultuurfonds (BNG Bank)\nLocation: Project must take place
  in Dutch municipalities\; projects largely abroad are excluded. Not regio
 n-restricted\, but 2026 priority goes to Limburg\, Overijssel\, Drenthe an
 d Zeeland.\nAward: EUR 5\,000 minimum to EUR 15\,000 maximum. The request 
 must represent 5 to 35 percent of total project funding\, so at least 65 p
 ercent co-financing is required. The fund is never the sole financier\, an
 d place-specific projects require at least one local or regional co-financ
 ier. No application fee.\nDuration: Single project with a clear start and 
 end\; must be executed within two years of award. A grantee cannot reapply
  for 36 months.\n\nMore: https://www.bngbank.nl/bng-cultuurfonds/projectsu
 bsidies?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.bngbank.nl/bng-cultuurfonds/projectsubsidies?utm_source=art
 ificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Project must take place in Dutch municipalities\; projects largely
  abroad are excluded. Not region-restricted\, but 2026 priority goes to Li
 mburg\, Overijssel\, Drenthe and Zeeland.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:cultuur-eindhoven-projecten-2027-r1@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260831T203817Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260930
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261001
SUMMARY:Deadline: Stichting Cultuur Eindhoven: Project Subsidy (Projecten\,
  2027 round 1)
DESCRIPTION:The mid-size project strand of Stichting Cultuur Eindhoven\, th
 e arm's-length body that distributes the city's culture budget\, and the m
 ain municipal route for an Eindhoven organisation to fund a festival\, exh
 ibition or public programme. Awards go up to EUR 35\,000 and cover a maxim
 um of 80 percent of eligible costs\, so at least a fifth of the budget mus
 t come from elsewhere. Unlike the Snelgeld strand this route is closed to 
 individuals: only private-law legal entities established in Eindhoven may 
 apply. Rounds run three times a year in fixed windows\; the next opens 1 S
 eptember and closes at 17:00 on 30 September 2026\, which is round 1 of th
 e 2027 cycle. TIMING: the decision lag is long by municipal standards at u
 p to 13 weeks after the submission window closes\, so a September 2026 app
 lication is decided around the end of December 2026 and activity should be
  planned for 2027. Given Eindhoven's design and technology profile\, media
 -art\, design and creative-technology programming fits the remit particula
 rly well. The parallel Snelgeld strand offers up to EUR 5\,000 on rolling 
 intake\, reopening 1 September 2026 and running until 31 December 2026 or 
 until the tranche budget is exhausted\, whichever comes first.\n\nOrganisa
 tion: Stichting Cultuur Eindhoven\nLocation: Eindhoven. The applicant must
  be a legal entity based in Eindhoven and the activity must serve the Eind
 hoven cultural offering. City-restricted at the applicant level.\nAward: M
 aximum EUR 35\,000 per application and maximum 80 percent of eligible cost
 s\, so at least 20 percent co-financing is required. No application fee.\n
 Duration: Single project within the 2025-2028 policy period.\n\nMore: http
 s://cultuureindhoven.nl/informatie-over-subsidies-2025-2028/?utm_source=ar
 tificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://cultuureindhoven.nl/informatie-over-subsidies-2025-2028/?utm_so
 urce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Eindhoven. The applicant must be a legal entity based in Eindhoven
  and the activity must serve the Eindhoven cultural offering. City-restric
 ted at the applicant level.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:gemeente-den-haag-kunst-cultuurprojecten-b-2026@artificialnouveau.githu
 b.io
DTSTAMP:20260831T203817Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261015
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261016
SUMMARY:Deadline: Gemeente Den Haag: Arts and Culture Projects Category B (
 autumn 2026 round)
DESCRIPTION:The larger of The Hague's two municipal project bands and the a
 ppropriate route for an organisation running a festival or substantial pub
 lic programme in the city. Awards range from EUR 10\,000 to 30\,000 agains
 t an annual ceiling of EUR 600\,000 for the whole strand. THE CO-FINANCING
  REQUIREMENT IS SEVERE and is the single most important planning constrain
 t: the municipal culture budget may fund at most 30 percent of the total p
 roject budget\, so an applicant seeking EUR 30\,000 must already have roug
 hly EUR 70\,000 secured or plausibly projected elsewhere. Only legal entit
 ies may apply\; individuals and informal collectives must use Category A i
 nstead (EUR 2\,000 to 10\,000\, 70 percent coverage ceiling\, next window 
 1 to 15 September 2026). Professional arts and culture organisations runni
 ng public projects in music\, theatre\, dance\, film\, literature\, visual
  arts or combinations are eligible. The next window opens 1 October and cl
 oses at 17:00 on 15 October 2026. TIMING: the decision term is 12 weeks af
 ter the window closes\, so an October 2026 application is decided around e
 arly January 2027 and activity should be scheduled from 2027 onward. Appli
 cations are handled through the municipality's subsidy system\, which migr
 ated to Easyfunders in April 2026. This scheme is independent of Stroom De
 n Haag. The underlying regulation runs to 31 December 2028.\n\nOrganisatio
 n: Gemeente Den Haag (Municipality of The Hague)\nLocation: The Hague. App
 licant must be active in Den Haag and the project must be publicly accessi
 ble there. City-restricted.\nAward: EUR 10\,000 to 30\,000 per application
 . The municipal culture-budget contribution may not exceed 30 percent of t
 he total project budget\, so at least 70 percent co-financing is required.
  Annual ceiling for the strand is EUR 600\,000. No application fee.\nDurat
 ion: Maximum one year per project.\n\nMore: https://www.denhaag.nl/nl/subs
 idies/subsidies-cultuur-en-evenementen/subsidie-kunst-en-cultuurprojecten-
 aanvragen/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.denhaag.nl/nl/subsidies/subsidies-cultuur-en-evenementen/su
 bsidie-kunst-en-cultuurprojecten-aanvragen/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugr
 antdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:The Hague. Applicant must be active in Den Haag and the project mu
 st be publicly accessible there. City-restricted.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:norma-fonds-projectbijdrage-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260831T203817Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261030
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261031
SUMMARY:Deadline: Stichting NORMA: NORMA Fonds Project Grant (round 4\, 202
 6)
DESCRIPTION:The NORMA Fonds redistributes copyright remuneration collected 
 by Stichting NORMA into cultural\, social and professional projects involv
 ing performing artists\, and is one of the few Dutch schemes with four int
 akes a year and a genuinely short cycle. Both arts-sector organisations an
 d individual arts professionals may apply\, though the applicant needs a b
 ank account and legal footing and cannot be a BIS-funded institution. The 
 project must centre on performing artists in the copyright sense\, meaning
  people who perform a copyright-protected work: musicians\, dancers\, acto
 rs\, voice actors. This fits live experimental music\, sound performance a
 nd performative media-art work\, but not object-based exhibitions or non-p
 erformative installation programmes. The maximum grant is EUR 10\,000\, th
 e total project budget must stay under EUR 150\,000\, the applicant's annu
 al budget under EUR 500\,000\, and at least a quarter of the project budge
 t must be earned from audience income\, so this is a top-up rather than a 
 primary funding source. Budgets must honour NORMA's 2026 performer wage no
 rms. Applications are submitted online during a one-month window each quar
 ter\; the next round runs 1 to 30 October 2026\, closing at 23:59. TIMING 
 RULE: decisions arrive no later than eight weeks after the deadline\, and 
 the premiere date must fall at least eight weeks after the application dea
 dline. Organisations that already received a NORMA Fonds grant in 2024 or 
 2025 are excluded\, and supporting staff may not exceed 2 FTE.\n\nOrganisa
 tion: Stichting NORMA (collecting society for performing artists)\nLocatio
 n: Netherlands-based arts-sector activity. No city or region restriction s
 tated.\nAward: Maximum EUR 10\,000 per project. Total project budget may n
 ot exceed EUR 150\,000 and the applicant organisation's annual budget may 
 not exceed EUR 500\,000. At least 25 percent of the project budget must co
 me from audience or box-office revenue. Performer fees must meet the 2026 
 wage norms of EUR 139 per rehearsal and EUR 340 per performance. No applic
 ation fee.\nDuration: Single project\, typically a production or concert s
 eries. Final report due within six months of completion.\n\nMore: https://
 www.stichtingnorma.nl/norma-fonds/aanvragen/?utm_source=artificialnouveaug
 rantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.stichtingnorma.nl/norma-fonds/aanvragen/?utm_source=artific
 ialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Netherlands-based arts-sector activity. No city or region restrict
 ion stated.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:kulturstiftung-des-bundes-general-project-funding-2026@artificialnouvea
 u.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260831T203817Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260731
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260801
SUMMARY:Deadline: Kulturstiftung des Bundes: General Project Funding (Allge
 meine Projektfoerderung)
DESCRIPTION:Germany's flagship open\, non-thematic federal project line\, a
 nd one of the largest European funders that will back a festival\, exhibit
 ion programme or multi-partner convening run by an organisation rather tha
 n an individual artist. It funds large innovative projects across all arti
 stic fields\, explicitly including New Media alongside visual and performi
 ng arts\, music\, film\, photography and architecture. There is no publish
 ed maximum\, but the EUR 50\,000 minimum total project cost sets the scale
 \, and at least 20 percent co-financing is mandatory. Deadlines are twice 
 yearly at 12:00 CET: 31 July 2026 and 31 January 2027. TIMING RULE: decisi
 ons are made by an external jury meeting in May and November\, and no proj
 ect may start before its jury date\, so plan four to six months of lead ti
 me. Non-German organisations are genuinely eligible\, which is unusual at 
 this scale\, provided the project is visible in Germany and has an interna
 tional dimension. Two practical barriers: the application form must be com
 pleted in German\, and project communications must include a German-langua
 ge version.\n\nOrganisation: Kulturstiftung des Bundes (German Federal Cul
 tural Foundation)\nLocation: Activity must be visible to audiences in Germ
 any. Institutions headquartered in Germany or abroad may apply.\nAward: No
  fixed ceiling\, but total project costs must exceed EUR 50\,000 to be eli
 gible. The Foundation allocates up to EUR 10 million per year across this 
 line. At least 20 percent of total project costs must be secured from own 
 capital and/or third-party funding. No application fee.\nDuration: Project
 -length. Projects may not begin before the jury meeting.\n\nMore: https://
 www.kulturstiftung-des-bundes.de/en/themes_focuses/general_project_funding
 .html?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.kulturstiftung-des-bundes.de/en/themes_focuses/general_proj
 ect_funding.html?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Activity must be visible to audiences in Germany. Institutions hea
 dquartered in Germany or abroad may apply.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:terra-foundation-collections-grants-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260831T203817Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260803
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260804
SUMMARY:Deadline: Terra Foundation for American Art: Collections Grants (20
 26 cycle)
DESCRIPTION:Funds organisations to reinstall permanent collections or mount
  temporary exhibitions drawn primarily from their own holdings\, on condit
 ion the project broadens understandings of American art and pursues inclus
 ive\, expansive curatorial practice. Planning grants of USD 25\,000 to 75\
 ,000 cover research\, advisory committees and conservation\; implementatio
 n grants up to USD 100\,000 cover interpretation\, exhibition design\, con
 servation\, public programmes and dissemination of research\, so the publi
 c-programming layer of an exhibition is fundable here. TIMING: the 2026 cy
 cle is two-stage\, with a grant inquiry due 3 August 2026\, a full proposa
 l for shortlisted applicants due 13 October 2026\, external panel review\,
  decisions in April 2027 and projects starting after 1 May 2027. That is a
  nine-month decision lag\, so this is planning-horizon money. Internationa
 l applicants are explicitly welcomed and need US 501(c)(3) status or the i
 nternational equivalent. The Foundation will not fund acquisitions\, equip
 ment\, exclusively online projects\, or projects consisting primarily of l
 oans. The American-art subject requirement is the main constraint for medi
 a-arts organisations.\n\nOrganisation: Terra Foundation for American Art\n
 Location: Worldwide. Museums\, art centres and community-based cultural or
 ganisations both inside and outside the US.\nAward: Planning grants USD 25
 \,000 to 75\,000 (conservation capped at 25 percent of a planning award)\;
  implementation grants up to USD 100\,000. No formal match\, but the Found
 ation prefers not to be sole funder. No application fee.\nDuration: Projec
 t-based\; funded projects start after 1 May 2027 following April 2027 deci
 sions.\n\nMore: https://www.terraamericanart.org/what-we-offer/grant-progr
 am/collections-grants/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=re
 ferral
URL:https://www.terraamericanart.org/what-we-offer/grant-program/collection
 s-grants/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Worldwide. Museums\, art centres and community-based cultural orga
 nisations both inside and outside the US.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:warhol-foundation-exhibition-support-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260831T203817Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260901
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260902
SUMMARY:Deadline: Andy Warhol Foundation: Exhibition Support (Fall 2026 rou
 nd)
DESCRIPTION:Supports solo\, two-person and thematic group exhibitions of co
 ntemporary visual art. The Foundation explicitly prioritises artists whose
  work is under-recognised and whose practices are experimental or hard to 
 categorise\, which makes it a genuine route for media arts\, digital cultu
 re and art-and-science exhibitions rather than a blue-chip-only fund. Gran
 ts of USD 60\,000 to 100\,000 cover direct exhibition costs including arti
 st fees\, new commissions\, catalogue production and artist-designed publi
 c programming\, but not staff salaries. Applicants may request no more tha
 n 25 percent of total direct costs. The proposal is a roughly three-page c
 uratorial letter plus detailed direct-cost budget\, organisational budget 
 and IRS documentation. Deadlines are 1 March and 1 September annually\, wi
 th notifications 1 July and 1 January. IMPORTANT: this is a postmark or em
 ail-timestamp deadline\, not a portal deadline. Fiscal sponsors are explic
 itly not accepted\; the applicant must hold its own IRS ruling letter. The
  six-month-to-two-year timing rule is strict\, so a September 2026 applica
 tion suits exhibitions programmed from mid-2027 onward.\n\nOrganisation: T
 he Andy Warhol Foundation for the Visual Arts\nLocation: Applicant's own v
 enue. US-based 501(c)(3) required\; international organisations must first
  submit a letter of inquiry before any proposal is accepted.\nAward: USD 6
 0\,000 to 100\,000. Direct costs only (artist payments\, catalogue and pub
 lication\, artist-designed public programmes)\; staff salaries excluded. R
 equest must not exceed 25 percent of total direct project costs\, which fu
 nctions as a de facto 75 percent co-financing requirement. No application 
 fee.\nDuration: Exhibition must open between 6 months and 2 years after no
 tification.\n\nMore: https://warholfoundation.org/grants/application-guide
 lines/exhibition-support/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium
 =referral
URL:https://warholfoundation.org/grants/application-guidelines/exhibition-s
 upport/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Applicant's own venue. US-based 501(c)(3) required\; international
  organisations must first submit a letter of inquiry before any proposal i
 s accepted.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:warhol-foundation-multiyear-program-support-2026@artificialnouveau.gith
 ub.io
DTSTAMP:20260831T203817Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260901
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260902
SUMMARY:Deadline: Andy Warhol Foundation: Multi-year Program Support (Fall 
 2026 round)
DESCRIPTION:This is the closest thing in US foundation philanthropy to core
  support for an organisation running an ongoing public programme\, as oppo
 sed to a single exhibition. It funds a two-year slate of exhibitions\, res
 idencies\, public art\, screenings\, performances\, lectures and publicati
 ons\, which means a recurring festival or convening series can be underwri
 tten here. Grants are USD 60\,000 to 100\,000 over two years and may not e
 xceed 25 percent of annual operating budget. The Foundation states a prefe
 rence for organisations supporting artists with experimental\, hard-to-cat
 egorise practices\, putting digital culture\, sound art and art-and-scienc
 e programmers squarely in scope. Applications require a forward programme 
 schedule covering at least the twelve months after the award\, a three-pag
 e narrative focused specifically on how artists benefit (the stated centra
 l evaluation criterion)\, a full one-year organisational budget and 501(c)
 (3) documentation. Deadlines are 1 March and 1 September\, notifications 1
  July and 1 January. Fiscal sponsors are not accepted. Organisations that 
 received a Multi-year grant within the past year are ineligible\, and prop
 osals centred on anniversaries\, relocations or major renovations are expl
 icitly discouraged.\n\nOrganisation: The Andy Warhol Foundation for the Vi
 sual Arts\nLocation: Programming delivered by the applicant organisation. 
 US 501(c)(3) required\; international organisations must submit a letter o
 f inquiry first.\nAward: USD 60\,000 to 100\,000 across two years. Request
  must not exceed 25 percent of the organisation's annual operating budget.
  No formal match\, but the 25 percent cap means the balance must come from
  elsewhere. No application fee.\nDuration: Two years of programming\, begi
 nning after the 1 January 2027 notification.\n\nMore: https://warholfounda
 tion.org/grants/application-guidelines/multi-year-program-support/?utm_sou
 rce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://warholfoundation.org/grants/application-guidelines/multi-year-p
 rogram-support/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Programming delivered by the applicant organisation. US 501(c)(3) 
 required\; international organisations must submit a letter of inquiry fir
 st.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:warhol-foundation-small-scale-project-grants-2026@artificialnouveau.git
 hub.io
DTSTAMP:20260831T203817Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260901
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260902
SUMMARY:Deadline: Andy Warhol Foundation: Project Grants for Small-Scale Or
 ganizations (Fall 2026 round)
DESCRIPTION:Launched in February 2026 as an expansion of the Foundation's p
 rogramme to reach organisations too small for the Exhibition Support and M
 ulti-year strands\, and it is the single most relevant new US scheme for s
 mall media-arts festivals. It funds visual arts projects with a public com
 ponent\, explicitly naming film festivals\, exhibitions\, installations\, 
 residencies and interdisciplinary collaborations. Grants are USD 20\,000 t
 o 30\,000 toward direct costs. The hard gate is the USD 200\,000 annual op
 erating budget ceiling plus US 501(c)(3) status held directly by the appli
 cant\, not via a fiscal sponsor. The Foundation states it assesses creativ
 e risk-taking and the growth of participating artists rather than communit
 y impact metrics\, which suits experimental sound and digital culture prog
 ramming. Proposals are a maximum of three pages plus a one-year operating 
 budget\, a project budget and IRS documentation. Deadlines are 1 March (pr
 ojects begin 1 July or later) and 1 September (projects begin 1 January or
  later). Youth-focused projects are ineligible. One project per round\, an
 d grantees must wait a year after project completion and final reporting b
 efore reapplying.\n\nOrganisation: The Andy Warhol Foundation for the Visu
 al Arts\nLocation: Applicant's own venue or programme\, with a mandatory p
 ublic component. US-based only.\nAward: USD 20\,000 to 30\,000 toward dire
 ct costs such as artist payments and production. No application fee.\nDura
 tion: Project must complete within one year of notification\; September-ro
 und projects may begin 1 January 2027 or later.\n\nMore: https://warholfou
 ndation.org/grants/application-guidelines/project-grants-for-small-scale-o
 rganizations/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://warholfoundation.org/grants/application-guidelines/project-gran
 ts-for-small-scale-organizations/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&ut
 m_medium=referral
LOCATION:Applicant's own venue or programme\, with a mandatory public compo
 nent. US-based only.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:creative-australia-arts-projects-organisations-2026@artificialnouveau.g
 ithub.io
DTSTAMP:20260831T203817Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260901
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260902
SUMMARY:Deadline: Creative Australia: Arts Projects for Organisations (Sept
 ember 2026 round)
DESCRIPTION:Creative Australia's principal open-round project grant for art
 s organisations and the most directly relevant Australian scheme for mount
 ing festivals\, exhibitions and public programmes. The guidelines explicit
 ly list festivals\, productions\, exhibitions\, performances\, touring\, p
 ublishing\, recording\, collaborations\, research and community engagement
  as supported activity. Organisations may propose either a single project 
 or an entire programme of projects\, which can extend to a full artistic p
 rogramme for a given calendar year or longer\, so this can function as de 
 facto annual programme funding. The category is artform-agnostic and routi
 nely supports media arts\, digital culture\, experimental sound and art-an
 d-science work\; activity delivered online is explicitly permitted. NOTABL
 E: international organisations are eligible where the project demonstrably
  benefits practising Australian artists\, their work\, or Australian audie
 nces\, so a non-Australian festival can apply if it is programming Austral
 ian artists. The applicant must be a legally constituted entity: incorpora
 ted association\, company limited by guarantee\, or government statutory a
 uthority. Registration in the Application Management System must be comple
 ted at least one business day before the closing date. The round closes 1 
 September 2026 at 3pm AEST.\n\nOrganisation: Creative Australia\nLocation:
  Activity may take place nationally within Australia\, internationally\, o
 r online.\nAward: AUD 20\,000 to 100\,000. No matching or co-financing req
 uirement. No application fee. Organisational administrative costs should g
 enerally not exceed 10 percent of the total project budget or the applicat
 ion becomes less competitive.\nDuration: Activity must last no longer than
  two years from the proposed start date\; the project must commence after 
 notification and within one year of it.\n\nMore: https://creative.gov.au/i
 nvestments-opportunities/arts-projects-organisations?utm_source=artificial
 nouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://creative.gov.au/investments-opportunities/arts-projects-organis
 ations?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Activity may take place nationally within Australia\, internationa
 lly\, or online.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:nordic-culture-point-network-funding-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260831T203817Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260904
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260905
SUMMARY:Deadline: Nordic Culture Point: Short-term Network Funding\, Nordic
 -Baltic Mobility Programme (autumn 2026)
DESCRIPTION:Supports organisations building new cross-border professional n
 etworks\, funding joint meetings\, workshops\, staff exchanges and collabo
 rative platforms among artists and cultural practitioners. It is designed 
 for the convening and infrastructure-building side of festival work rather
  than artistic production\, and it explicitly excludes artistic production
 s and public events\, so it is used to assemble festival partners rather t
 han to stage the festival itself. Grants run up to EUR 20\,000 for network
 s of a year or less\, with Nordic Culture Point covering at most 70 percen
 t of the budget and a hard 85 percent ceiling on combined pan-Nordic publi
 c funding. The autumn 2026 window is 10 August to 4 September 2026\, closi
 ng 15:59 UTC+3. TIMING RULE: activity may not begin until at least eight w
 eeks after the deadline. IMPORTANT ELIGIBILITY DIFFERENCE from the Culture
  and Art Programme: the applicant must be resident in a Nordic or Baltic c
 ountry and must be a professional with documented training or experience i
 n art and culture\, so non-Nordic and non-Baltic lead applicants are not e
 ligible. A strong fit for a media-arts or sound-art organisation assemblin
 g a regional partner consortium ahead of a larger application. WHO CAN APP
 LY: 'Applications may be submitted by individuals or organisations.' Indiv
 iduals must be resident in a Nordic or Baltic country\, though citizenship
  is not required. Groups\, organisations and institutions must be register
 ed in a Nordic or Baltic country\, so an unregistered collective would nee
 d a registered partner to act as applicant.\n\nOrganisation: Nordic Cultur
 e Point (Kulturkontakt Nord)\nLocation: Nordic and Baltic region. The netw
 ork must include partners from at least three of: Denmark\, Estonia\, Finl
 and\, Faroe Islands\, Greenland\, Iceland\, Latvia\, Lithuania\, Norway\, 
 Sweden\, Aland.\nAward: Up to EUR 20\,000 for networks lasting one year or
  less. Nordic Culture Point covers a maximum of 70 percent of the project 
 budget\, and combined funding from this programme plus other pan-Nordic bo
 dies may not exceed 85 percent\, so at least 15 percent must come from oth
 er sources. No application fee.\nDuration: Up to one year. Activity may st
 art no earlier than eight weeks after the deadline.\n\nMore: https://www.n
 kk.org/en/grants/short-term-network-funding/?utm_source=artificialnouveaug
 rantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.nkk.org/en/grants/short-term-network-funding/?utm_source=ar
 tificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Nordic and Baltic region. The network must include partners from a
 t least three of: Denmark\, Estonia\, Finland\, Faroe Islands\, Greenland\
 , Iceland\, Latvia\, Lithuania\, Norway\, Sweden\, Aland.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:teiger-foundation-hosting-grant-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260831T203817Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260909
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260910
SUMMARY:Deadline: Teiger Foundation: Hosting Grant (September 2026 quarterl
 y deadline)
DESCRIPTION:Funds US organisations to present curator-led contemporary visu
 al art exhibitions and projects that originated elsewhere\, on condition t
 he presenting institution meaningfully adapts the project to its own conte
 xt. Teiger's remit covers group exhibitions\, single-artist surveys\, part
 icipatory and community-engaged projects\, digital exhibitions\, and live 
 and virtual performance\, making it one of very few US funders that will d
 irectly finance media-art and performance programming at organisational le
 vel. Requests are fixed at USD 50\,000 or USD 75\,000 with up to 30 percen
 t for indirect costs\, and there is no minimum organisation budget size\, 
 with smaller organisations explicitly favoured for infrastructure support.
  Hosting deadlines are quarterly: 9 September 2026 and 9 December 2026\, b
 oth 17:00 ET\, each mapped to a defined project-opening window roughly a y
 ear out. IMPORTANT: re-presenting a touring project unchanged is explicitl
 y not competitive\; the curatorial adaptation is the substance of the appl
 ication. US 501(c)(3) status is required and the fund is not open to indiv
 iduals or non-US organisations. Teiger's larger biennial Call for Proposal
 s is not running in 2026 and next opens in autumn 2026 with an early-2027 
 deadline.\n\nOrganisation: Teiger Foundation\nLocation: United States. The
  presenting organisation must be US-based\, though the originating project
  may have come from anywhere in the world.\nAward: USD 50\,000 or USD 75\,
 000 (fixed request tiers\, applicant chooses). Up to 30 percent may cover 
 indirect and overhead costs. Organisations with annual budgets under USD 3
 .5 million receive special consideration for infrastructure costs. No matc
 hing requirement. No application fee.\nDuration: Roughly 12 months\; the 9
  September 2026 deadline covers projects opening between 1 April 2027 and 
 31 March 2028.\n\nMore: https://teigerfoundation.org/what-we-fund-how-to-a
 pply/hosting?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://teigerfoundation.org/what-we-fund-how-to-apply/hosting?utm_sour
 ce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:United States. The presenting organisation must be US-based\, thou
 gh the originating project may have come from anywhere in the world.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:nordic-culture-point-culture-art-programme-2026@artificialnouveau.githu
 b.io
DTSTAMP:20260831T203817Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260910
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260911
SUMMARY:Deadline: Nordic Culture Point: Culture and Art Programme (autumn 2
 026 round)
DESCRIPTION:Nordic Culture Point's main project line\, funding Nordic colla
 borative arts and culture projects across all phases: preliminary work\, p
 roduction\, presentation and dissemination. Eligible activity explicitly i
 ncludes creative productions\, workshops\, knowledge development and space
 s for artists to meet publics\, which covers festivals\, public programmes
  and convenings when framed as new collaborations. The tiered co-financing
  model is the standout feature: EUR 7\,000 with no match at all\, rising t
 o EUR 100\,000 at a 50 percent match\, and in-kind contributions count. NO
 TABLE: applicants do not need Nordic residency or citizenship provided the
  three-country and two-Nordic partner structure is met\, so a non-Nordic o
 rganisation can lead the project. The autumn window runs 10 August to 10 S
 eptember 2026\, closing 15:59 UTC+3. TIMING RULE: decisions arrive ten wee
 ks after the deadline and no project may start before notification\, so bu
 dget for a roughly three-month lag. The programme will not finance existin
 g tours\, institutional running costs\, ongoing festival core financing\, 
 solo performances\, film\, TV or gaming production\, or book publishing\, 
 so a recurring festival must present a distinct new collaborative strand r
 ather than seek operating support. WHO CAN APPLY: the programme states tha
 t 'anyone within the field of art and culture can apply'\, as long as the 
 project meets the criteria and is realised through co-operation with partn
 ers from at least three countries\, at least two of them Nordic. Individua
 ls and artist groups are eligible alongside organisations\; there is no re
 quirement to be a registered legal entity.\n\nOrganisation: Nordic Culture
  Point (Kulturkontakt Nord)\nLocation: Activity may take place anywhere\, 
 but the project must involve partners with addresses in at least three dif
 ferent countries\, at least two of which are Nordic (Denmark\, Finland\, I
 celand\, Norway\, Sweden\, Faroe Islands\, Greenland\, Aland).\nAward: Tie
 red by co-financing: up to EUR 7\,000 with NO co-funding required\; up to 
 EUR 40\,000 with at least 30 percent co-funding\; up to EUR 100\,000 with 
 at least 50 percent co-funding. In-kind goods and services count toward co
 -financing. No application fee.\nDuration: Project-based. Funded activity 
 may only begin after decision notification\, roughly ten weeks after the d
 eadline.\n\nMore: https://www.nkk.org/en/grants/culture-and-art-programme/
 ?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.nkk.org/en/grants/culture-and-art-programme/?utm_source=art
 ificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Activity may take place anywhere\, but the project must involve pa
 rtners with addresses in at least three different countries\, at least two
  of which are Nordic (Denmark\, Finland\, Iceland\, Norway\, Sweden\, Faro
 e Islands\, Greenland\, Aland).
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:terra-foundation-convening-grants-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260831T203817Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260928
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260929
SUMMARY:Deadline: Terra Foundation for American Art: Convening Grants (Roun
 d 1\, 2026-27)
DESCRIPTION:The most directly relevant Terra line for organisations running
  convenings rather than exhibitions: conversations\, symposia and workshop
 s that stimulate interdisciplinary and intercultural exchange. Covered cos
 ts are unusually broad and practical\, including professional fees\, artis
 t honoraria\, travel\, AV support\, interpretation and translation\, cater
 ing\, research dissemination\, marketing\, and administrative costs up to 
 20 percent. Awards run USD 10\,000 to 25\,000 and are made twice yearly. T
 he process is two-stage: Round 1 has a grant inquiry due 28 September 2026
  followed\, if invited\, by a full proposal due 30 November 2026\, for pro
 grammes taking place after 1 May 2027. Round 2 has an inquiry due 16 Febru
 ary 2027 and proposal due 20 April 2027 for programmes after 1 November 20
 27. Invited proposals go to an external panel of curators and arts profess
 ionals. International applicants are explicitly eligible and need US 501(c
 )(3) status or a recognised non-profit equivalent in their own country. Th
 e binding constraint is topical rather than geographic: a European or Asia
 n organisation can win this\, but the convening must engage American or In
 digenous North American visual art\, which is a workable frame for art-and
 -technology or sound-art programming with a US axis.\n\nOrganisation: Terr
 a Foundation for American Art\nLocation: Worldwide. Open to organisations 
 anywhere\, but subject matter must relate to the visual arts of the United
  States or Indigenous arts of North America.\nAward: USD 10\,000 to 25\,00
 0. Administrative costs capped at 20 percent of the grant. No formal match
  required\, but the Foundation prefers not to be sole funder. No applicati
 on fee.\nDuration: Event-based\; Round 1 supports programmes taking place 
 after 1 May 2027.\n\nMore: https://www.terraamericanart.org/what-we-offer/
 grant-program/convening-grants/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_
 medium=referral
URL:https://www.terraamericanart.org/what-we-offer/grant-program/convening-
 grants/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Worldwide. Open to organisations anywhere\, but subject matter mus
 t relate to the visual arts of the United States or Indigenous arts of Nor
 th America.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:canada-council-circulation-touring-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260831T203817Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261007
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261008
SUMMARY:Deadline: Canada Council for the Arts: Arts Across Canada and Abroa
 d\, Circulation and Touring (October 2026 round)
DESCRIPTION:Funds the circulation and touring of artists\, exhibitions and 
 artistic works by artists\, groups and organisations from Canada\, nationa
 lly and internationally. Media arts\, digital arts and new media\, inter-a
 rts\, and music and sound art are all explicitly named as supported practi
 ces\, so experimental sound and creative technology work is in scope. This
  component sits inside Arts Across Canada and Abroad\, the merged programm
 e introduced in 2025 that replaced the separate Arts Across Canada and Art
 s Abroad programmes\; the old Digital Now programme is discontinued. IMPOR
 TANT AND UNDERUSED: non-Canadian organisations are eligible via the Foreig
 n arts festival\, biennale or book fair profile\, defined as an incorporat
 ed organisation headquartered outside Canada running an international medi
 a arts festival\, an international literary or storytelling festival\, an 
 international book fair\, or a major international visual arts biennial\, 
 triennial or quinquennial. That support is restricted to presenting Canadi
 an media\, literary or visual artists and their work\, and it is not adver
 tised on the programme page. For digital and media arts\, requests must be
  for work independent of the commercial film\, television and video game i
 ndustries\, and only the creator or director may apply\, not producers or 
 production companies. Deadlines run three times a year. The sister compone
 nt Representation and Promotion has continuous rolling intake and the same
  foreign-festival eligibility.\n\nOrganisation: Canada Council for the Art
 s\nLocation: Touring and circulation within Canada and internationally.\nA
 ward: CAD. Minimum and maximum are NOT published publicly\; amounts are di
 sclosed only inside the Council's client portal at arts-services.ca\, whic
 h requires a login. No application fee. Council funds cannot cover expense
 s already covered by another revenue source\, and combined municipal\, pro
 vincial and federal grants must demonstrate complementarity of public supp
 ort.\nDuration: Project-based\; results usually notified within 5 months o
 f the deadline.\n\nMore: https://canadacouncil.ca/funding/grants/arts-acro
 ss-canada-and-abroad?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=refe
 rral
URL:https://canadacouncil.ca/funding/grants/arts-across-canada-and-abroad?u
 tm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Touring and circulation within Canada and internationally.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:creative-australia-international-engagement-2026@artificialnouveau.gith
 ub.io
DTSTAMP:20260831T203817Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261013
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261014
SUMMARY:Deadline: Creative Australia: International Engagement Fund (Octobe
 r 2026 round)
DESCRIPTION:Supports reciprocal international exchange between Australian p
 ractitioners or organisations and confirmed overseas partners\, which make
 s it the right instrument for co-hosted convenings\, labs and cross-border
  programme partnerships rather than one-way touring. Supported activity ty
 pes are creative collaboration and development\, cultural exchange and kno
 wledge sharing\, and labs and practice-exchange models\, mapping closely o
 nto media arts residencies\, art-and-science research exchanges and digita
 l culture symposia. Eligible costs include artist fees\, travel\, accommod
 ation\, production expenses\, marketing\, access costs\, and childcare or 
 carer support. International organisations are eligible where the project 
 benefits Australian artists or creative workers\, and a confirmed internat
 ional partner is mandatory and must confirm participation in writing. The 
 reciprocity requirement is substantive: the strongest applications embed m
 utually beneficial exchange rather than simply presenting an Australian ar
 tist abroad. Creative Australia's published assessment feedback notes top-
 ranked applications foregrounded First Nations self-determined or diaspori
 c-led activity and demonstrated sector-wide impact. It is competitive: 157
  eligible applications in the March 2026 round yielded 33 grants\, about a
  21 percent success rate. Contemporary music practitioners are excluded an
 d directed to Music Australia programmes. Closes 13 October 2026 at 3pm AE
 DT. WHO CAN APPLY: 'individuals\, groups and organisations (including smal
 l businesses) may apply to this category.' Individual applicants must be a
 n Australian citizen or permanent resident. A legally constituted entity i
 s not required\, so unincorporated groups are eligible.\n\nOrganisation: C
 reative Australia\nLocation: International\, with a confirmed overseas par
 tner.\nAward: AUD 5\,000 to 30\,000. No application fee. No formal matchin
 g requirement\, but assessment explicitly weighs diversity and scale of in
 come and co-funding\, including earned income\, grants\, sponsorship and i
 n-kind contributions.\nDuration: Activities must not exceed two years from
  the proposed start date\; supported activity must fall between 1 July 202
 6 and 1 July 2028.\n\nMore: https://creative.gov.au/investments-opportunit
 ies/international-engagement-fund?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&ut
 m_medium=referral
URL:https://creative.gov.au/investments-opportunities/international-engagem
 ent-fund?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:International\, with a confirmed overseas partner.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:canada-council-public-outreach-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260831T203817Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261014
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261015
SUMMARY:Deadline: Canada Council for the Arts: Arts Across Canada and Abroa
 d\, Public Outreach (October 2026 round)
DESCRIPTION:Funds activities that build connections between artists and div
 erse audiences and contribute to public appreciation and enjoyment of the 
 arts in Canada. This is the closest Canada Council fit for running a publi
 c programme\, a single festival edition\, a talks series or audience-facin
 g exhibition programming\, as distinct from creating the artwork itself. I
 t is open to arts festivals\, presenters and event organisers under the Pr
 esenting organization profile\, alongside Artistic organizations\, Artisti
 c groups and Arts supporting groups\, and the profile explicitly includes 
 visual arts festivals\, biennials\, triennials and quinquennials. Digital 
 arts and new media\, media arts\, inter-arts\, and music and sound art are
  named among funded practices\, so experimental sound art and creative tec
 hnology programming qualify. IMPORTANT: unlike the Circulation and Touring
  component\, international organisations are NOT eligible for Public Outre
 ach. The Council will not fund projects whose primary focus is educational
 \, therapeutic\, recreational or social service delivery\, nor fundraising
  activities or prize and award ceremonies. Deadlines fall twice a year. Th
 e related Composite Activities component offers up to 3 years of support f
 or bundled multi-project programmes and may suit a recurring festival arc 
 better.\n\nOrganisation: Canada Council for the Arts\nLocation: Activities
  must build audiences and public appreciation of the arts in Canada. Organ
 isations must be incorporated or registered in Canada.\nAward: CAD. Minimu
 m and maximum are NOT published publicly\; disclosed only in the client po
 rtal at arts-services.ca\, which requires a login. No application fee. Cou
 ncil funds cannot cover expenses already covered by another revenue source
 \; combined public grants must demonstrate complementarity.\nDuration: Pro
 ject-based\; results usually notified within 5 months of the deadline.\n\n
 More: https://canadacouncil.ca/funding/grants/arts-across-canada-and-abroa
 d?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://canadacouncil.ca/funding/grants/arts-across-canada-and-abroad?u
 tm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Activities must build audiences and public appreciation of the art
 s in Canada. Organisations must be incorporated or registered in Canada.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:japan-foundation-exhibitions-abroad-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260831T203817Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261201
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261202
SUMMARY:Deadline: The Japan Foundation: Exhibitions Abroad Support Program 
 (FY2027-28 round)
DESCRIPTION:The Japan Foundation's flagship grant for organisations abroad 
 mounting an exhibition introducing Japanese art and culture\, explicitly c
 overing overseas biennials and triennials that present Japanese artists. I
 t is a partial-cost grant rather than a production budget: it pays toward 
 shipping Japanese works\, producing print or digital catalogues\, and brin
 ging Japanese artists\, curators and specialists to the venue. That cost s
 tructure suits media arts\, digital culture and art-and-science exhibition
 s well\, where shipping technical work and hosting the artist for installa
 tion are the main cost drivers. It is explicitly designed for non-Japanese
  applicants: museums\, galleries and comparable organisations outside Japa
 n. Institutions only\, so independent curators and artists cannot apply di
 rectly and must be hosted by an eligible institution. Exhibition content m
 ust introduce Japanese art and culture\, so a Japanese artistic component 
 is mandatory. Recent UK recipients include Tate Modern\, the V&A and the H
 ayward Gallery\, so the scheme skews toward established institutions. Appl
 icants are asked to discuss eligibility with the relevant regional arts pr
 ogramme officer before applying. FLAG: full FY2027 guidelines were not yet
  published by Tokyo headquarters as of July 2026 and this deadline is the 
 funder's own provisional date\; reconfirm in autumn 2026.\n\nOrganisation:
  The Japan Foundation\nLocation: Exhibition takes place at the applicant i
 nstitution's own venue outside Japan. National rounds run through Japan Fo
 undation offices worldwide.\nAward: No published ceiling. Partial-cost gra
 nt only: packing and shipping of Japanese exhibits (insurance excluded)\, 
 catalogue production including digital catalogues\, and travel for invited
  Japanese artists\, curators and specialists. Preliminary research and dev
 elopment explicitly excluded. The grant is partial by design\, so the host
  institution funds the balance. No application fee.\nDuration: Exhibitions
  must open between 1 April 2027 and 31 March 2028\; results notified April
  2027.\n\nMore: https://www.jpf.org.uk/artsandculture/funding.php?utm_sour
 ce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.jpf.org.uk/artsandculture/funding.php?utm_source=artificial
 nouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Exhibition takes place at the applicant institution's own venue ou
 tside Japan. National rounds run through Japan Foundation offices worldwid
 e.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:arts-council-wales-festivals-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260831T203817Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260729
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260730
SUMMARY:Deadline: Arts Council of Wales: Festivals (2026 rounds)
DESCRIPTION:Festivals is one of the new National Lottery programmes Arts Co
 uncil of Wales launched on 13 April 2026\, and it is the clearest organisa
 tion-facing route for funding a public festival in Wales. It supports focu
 sed\, time-limited festivals delivering high-quality arts programmes to br
 oad audiences\, in a single artform or mixed artforms\, with preference gi
 ven to festivals that commission\, create and present new artistic work. G
 rants run GBP 500 to 100\,000 across four tiers\, with the tier ceiling ti
 ed to how long the festival has been established. Match funding is mandato
 ry: the Council covers at most 75 percent of eligible costs and in-kind su
 pport is capped at 10 percent. There are two deadlines in 2026\, both at 1
 pm: Wednesday 29 July 2026 and Wednesday 16 December 2026. TIMING RULE: a 
 minimum of twelve working weeks must fall between the deadline and the pro
 ject start date\, so activity applied for in the July round cannot begin b
 efore roughly late October 2026. Retrospective costs are ineligible. Indiv
 idual artists cannot apply.\n\nOrganisation: Arts Council of Wales\nLocati
 on: Festival must take place in Wales and demonstrate cultural value to th
 e local community. Welsh language integration expected.\nAward: GBP 500 to
  100\,000 across four tiers: Small up to GBP 10\,000\; Large up to GBP 35\
 ,000 (1+ year track record)\; Large up to GBP 60\,000 (3+ years\, regional
  significance\, 2+ day programme)\; Large up to GBP 100\,000 (5+ years\, n
 ational significance). Co-financing mandatory: the Council funds a maximum
  of 75 percent of eligible costs\, so at least 25 percent of project incom
 e must come from non-Arts Council and non-Lottery sources\, of which no mo
 re than 10 percent may be in-kind. No application fee.\nDuration: One or t
 wo years of festival activity\; two-year applications require a track reco
 rd and development plan.\n\nMore: https://arts.wales/festivals-0?utm_sourc
 e=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://arts.wales/festivals-0?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&ut
 m_medium=referral
LOCATION:Festival must take place in Wales and demonstrate cultural value t
 o the local community. Welsh language integration expected.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:arts-council-wales-create-and-engage-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260831T203817Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260729
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260730
SUMMARY:Deadline: Arts Council of Wales: Create and Engage (2026 rounds)
DESCRIPTION:Create and Engage is Arts Council of Wales's general-purpose Na
 tional Lottery programme for making and presenting arts work\, launched al
 ongside Festivals in April 2026\, and is the natural fit for exhibitions\,
  public programmes\, touring and participatory events that are not structu
 red as a festival. It funds creation\, presentation\, programming\, tourin
 g\, community participation and\, for organisations only\, professional de
 velopment. Small awards go up to GBP 10\,000 and large awards run GBP 10\,
 001 to 60\,000\, with up to GBP 100\,000 possible in exceptional cases wit
 h advance manager approval. At least 10 percent of project costs must come
  from non-Council\, non-Lottery sources\, a notably lighter co-financing b
 urden than the Festivals fund's 25 percent. TIMING RULES: Small Create and
  Engage is rolling with no set deadlines but requires a minimum of 10 work
 ing weeks between submission and project start\; Large Create and Engage h
 as fixed 1pm deadlines on 29 July 2026\, 30 September 2026 and 16 December
  2026\, with a minimum of 12 working weeks between deadline and project st
 art. WHO CAN APPLY: both organisations and individuals\, though individual
  applicants must be based in Wales. Non-UK organisations can participate a
 s partners but cannot lead. Applicants cannot have an application in to mo
 re than one Arts Council fund at the same time.\n\nOrganisation: Arts Coun
 cil of Wales\nLocation: Projects must take place mainly in Wales. Individu
 al applicants must be Wales-based\; organisations outside the UK may take 
 part as partners provided a UK-based eligible organisation leads.\nAward: 
 Small awards up to GBP 10\,000\; Large awards GBP 10\,001 to 60\,000\; exc
 eptionally up to GBP 100\,000 with prior approval from an Arts Council man
 ager. At least 10 percent of project costs must come from non-Arts Council
  and non-Lottery sources. No application fee.\nDuration: Project-length\; 
 activity must not already be underway at the point of application.\n\nMore
 : https://arts.wales/funding/individuals/create-and-engage?utm_source=arti
 ficialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://arts.wales/funding/individuals/create-and-engage?utm_source=art
 ificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Projects must take place mainly in Wales. Individual applicants mu
 st be Wales-based\; organisations outside the UK may take part as partners
  provided a UK-based eligible organisation leads.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:acni-aidf-organisations-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260831T203817Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260730
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260731
SUMMARY:Deadline: Arts Council of Northern Ireland: Artists' International 
 Development Fund for Organisations (2026)
DESCRIPTION:The Artists' International Development Fund (Organisations) is 
 Arts Council of Northern Ireland's route for NI-based arts organisations t
 o take a first substantive step into international working. It is the orga
 nisations counterpart to the individual-artist AIDF under the Support for 
 the Individual Artist Programme\, which is a separate scheme with its own 
 amount band. Grants run GBP 1\,000 to 7\,000 and cover art materials\, res
 idency costs\, travel including airfare and mileage\, artistic and technic
 al fees for production or post-production\, venue hire\, and equipment cap
 ped at 50 percent of the request value. The deadline is Thursday 30 July 2
 026 at 12:00 noon\, and the online system closes precisely at noon. Applic
 ants must be NI-based\, must have received recognition for their work ther
 e\, and must not already have extensive international experience. The appl
 ication must evidence genuine interest from an overseas partner or host\, 
 so a confirmed international invitation\, residency offer or presentation 
 opportunity is effectively a precondition.\n\nOrganisation: Arts Council o
 f Northern Ireland\nLocation: Applicant organisations must be based in Nor
 thern Ireland\; the funded activity takes place internationally\, with an 
 overseas partner or host.\nAward: GBP 1\,000 to 7\,000. Covers art materia
 ls\, residency costs\, travel (mileage at 25.7p per mile plus airfare)\, a
 rtistic and technical fees for production or post-production\, venue hire\
 , project equipment capped at 50 percent of the request value\, and IT equ
 ipment up to GBP 1\,200 for laptops or GBP 500 for tablets. No application
  fee.\nDuration: Short\, early-stage international development activity.\n
 \nMore: https://artscouncil-ni.org/funding-for-organisations/artists-inter
 national-development-fund-organisations?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantd
 esk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://artscouncil-ni.org/funding-for-organisations/artists-internatio
 nal-development-fund-organisations?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&u
 tm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Applicant organisations must be based in Northern Ireland\; the fu
 nded activity takes place internationally\, with an overseas partner or ho
 st.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:acni-rural-engagement-arts-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260831T203817Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260924
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260925
SUMMARY:Deadline: Arts Council of Northern Ireland: National Lottery Rural 
 Engagement Arts Programme (2026)
DESCRIPTION:The National Lottery Rural Engagement Arts Programme funds orga
 nisations to deliver arts activity in rural Northern Ireland\, addressing 
 isolation and social inclusion. It supports either a single one-off projec
 t or a multi-event public programme\, making it usable for exhibitions\, w
 orkshops\, touring events and community-facing digital or media arts work.
  Grants range from GBP 500 to 10\,000\, covering artist fees\, transport\,
  materials\, venue hire\, accessibility support\, volunteer expenses\, eva
 luation\, and equipment up to 50 percent of the request value. The deadlin
 e is Thursday 24 September 2026 at 12:00 noon\, and the online system clos
 es precisely at noon with no late or incomplete submissions accepted. TIMI
 NG RULE: funded activity must fall between 1 December 2026 and 30 November
  2027\, setting an effective earliest start date of roughly ten weeks afte
 r the deadline. Registered charities\, formally constituted non-profit gro
 ups\, local authorities and arts organisations are eligible\, including bo
 dies based outside Northern Ireland where the benefit accrues to rural NI 
 residents. Consortium applications demonstrating partnership working are e
 xplicitly prioritised. The rural and community framing means creative-tech
 nology work qualifies only where framed for that audience.\n\nOrganisation
 : Arts Council of Northern Ireland\nLocation: Activity must target rural c
 ommunities in Northern Ireland per the NISRA 2015 settlement classificatio
 n. Organisations based outside Northern Ireland may apply if the project b
 enefits rural NI residents.\nAward: GBP 500 to 10\,000 per project. Eligib
 le costs include artist fees\, transport\, materials\, venue hire\, access
 ibility support\, equipment (capped at 50 percent of the request value)\, 
 volunteer expenses and evaluation. No application fee.\nDuration: Maximum 
 12 months\; activity must take place between 1 December 2026 and 30 Novemb
 er 2027.\n\nMore: https://artscouncil-ni.org/funding-for-organisations/rur
 al-engagement-arts-programme?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_med
 ium=referral
URL:https://artscouncil-ni.org/funding-for-organisations/rural-engagement-a
 rts-programme?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Activity must target rural communities in Northern Ireland per the
  NISRA 2015 settlement classification. Organisations based outside Norther
 n Ireland may apply if the project benefits rural NI residents.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:jerwood-foundation-arts-grants-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260831T203817Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270317
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270318
SUMMARY:Deadline: Jerwood Foundation: Arts Grants (2027 round)
DESCRIPTION:The Jerwood Foundation makes grants to UK organisations for pub
 lic-facing arts activity across theatre\, music\, dance\, visual arts and 
 literature\, including artist development programmes\, commissions\, resid
 encies and projects involving the Jerwood Collection. Awards have historic
 ally gone as high as GBP 200\,000\, though the Foundation states most gran
 ts are much smaller. Applications are single-stage: a written proposal of 
 no more than 10 sides of A4 excluding financial statements\, sent by email
  to info@jerwood.org or by post\, and it must include a summary sheet givi
 ng location\, amount requested\, timeline and audience figures. Applicatio
 ns missing that summary sheet are rejected automatically. The March 2026 d
 eadline has passed\; the next round opens 3 February 2027 at 9am and close
 s 17 March 2027 at 2pm\, with decisions on 28 April 2027 and all applicant
 s notified by 11 May 2027. TIMING RULE: activity funded in that round must
  start or open to the public between 1 July 2027 and 30 June 2028\, so the
 re is a long lead time and retrospective funding is impossible. Grants to 
 individuals are not made\, so artists must be supported through a host org
 anisation. Core costs and capital work are explicitly out of scope\, which
  makes this a good fit for discrete festivals\, exhibitions and public pro
 grammes.\n\nOrganisation: Jerwood Foundation\nLocation: United Kingdom. Ap
 plicants must be UK registered charities or UK limited companies.\nAward: 
 No published minimum or maximum. Previous awards have reached up to GBP 20
 0\,000\, but most grants are considerably smaller. Funds project and activ
 ity costs. No formal match-funding requirement\, but a fundraising strateg
 y must be submitted. No application fee.\nDuration: Activity for this roun
 d must start or open to the public between 1 July 2027 and 30 June 2028.\n
 \nMore: https://jerwood.org/funding/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk
 &utm_medium=referral
URL:https://jerwood.org/funding/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_
 medium=referral
LOCATION:United Kingdom. Applicants must be UK registered charities or UK l
 imited companies.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:arm-holding-commission-h-residence-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260831T203817Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260725
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260726
SUMMARY:Deadline: A.R.M. Holding / Art Dubai Projects: H Residence Sculptur
 e Park Commission (Dubai)
DESCRIPTION:A.R.M. Holding and HUNA\, with the commission supported and man
 aged by Art Dubai Projects\, invite artists to propose a permanent public 
 artwork for the H Residence Sculpture Park in Dubai\, the anchor piece of 
 the park's programme. Artists respond to the theme 'We Emerge Stronger tha
 n Before' through a permanent\, site-specific outdoor sculpture\; the stro
 ngest proposals will find what the phrase opens up (continuity\, endurance
 \, renewal\, collective presence\, the long view) through material\, form\
 , scale and the conditions of the site. Where language or text is incorpor
 ated\, Arabic should lead. TECHNICAL: footprint minimum around 15 sqm\, up
  to 3 m high\; weight restriction 5.5 kN/m2\; must be suitable for long-te
 rm outdoor display in Dubai (summer over 40 C\, humidity to 90 percent\, a
 bout six hours direct sun daily)\; presence by day and night. ELIGIBILITY:
  open to artists with or without gallery representation\; UAE-based\, regi
 onal and international artists welcome\; prior experience with permanent o
 r large-scale outdoor/public installation required. BUDGET: AED 1\,000\,00
 0 all-inclusive\; shortlisted artists receive full budget parameters and p
 roposal fees at the proposal development stage. SUBMISSION: CV and portfol
 io (attention to outdoor\, large-scale or permanent commissions)\, concept
  statement (max 300 words)\, a render or visualisation in context plus at 
 least one sketch\, technical specifications\, and a site response. TIMELIN
 E: submissions close 25 July 2026\; shortlist notified from 10 August\; co
 mmission awarded after September proposal development\; work unveiled at H
  Residence on 2 December 2026. Local fabrication strongly preferred. Quest
 ions: Shahad@artdubai.ae.\n\nOrganisation: A.R.M. Holding / HUNA / Art Dub
 ai Projects\nLocation: H Residence Sculpture Park\, Dubai\, UAE. Open to U
 AE-based\, regional and international artists.\nAward: AED 1\,000\,000 com
 mission envelope\, inclusive of artist fee\, design development\, fabricat
 ion\, materials\, production\, transport\, installation\, lighting and fin
 ishing. Proposal fees are available for shortlisted artists. No submission
  fee.\nDuration: Proposal development September 2026\; fabrication autumn 
 2026\; unveiling 2 December 2026\n\nMore: https://www.artdubai.ae/wp-conte
 nt/uploads/2026/06/ADP_ARM-HOLDING-COMMISSION_OPEN-CALL-PACK-.pdf?utm_sour
 ce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.artdubai.ae/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/ADP_ARM-HOLDING-COMM
 ISSION_OPEN-CALL-PACK-.pdf?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_mediu
 m=referral
LOCATION:H Residence Sculpture Park\, Dubai\, UAE. Open to UAE-based\, regi
 onal and international artists.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:wave-hill-van-lier-ankhlave-fellowship-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260831T203817Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260810
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260811
SUMMARY:Deadline: Wave Hill / AnkhLave Arts Alliance: 2027 Van Lier Fellows
 hip (NYC)
DESCRIPTION:Wave Hill\, in partnership with AnkhLave Arts Alliance\, invite
 s NYC-based artists who identify as BIPOC to apply for the 2027 Van Lier F
 ellowship as part of the 9th Annual AnkhLave Garden Project at Wave Hill P
 ublic Garden and Cultural Center in the Bronx. The project supports artist
 s who draw on research\, scholarship and lived knowledge to present site-r
 esponsive work at the intersection of nature\, culture and place\, engagin
 g with Wave Hill's plant collections\, history\, design and architecture. 
 The Van Lier Fellowship (funded by the Edward and Sally Van Lier Fund thro
 ugh the New York Community Trust) will be awarded to two NYC-based visual 
 artists aged 30 or younger. FELLOWSHIP: participation in the Winter Worksp
 ace residency (23 February - 18 April 2027)\; a $10\,435 stipend including
  an $8\,000 honorarium and transportation stipend\; a solo exhibition in t
 he Sunroom or Sun Porch (15 May - 4 July 2027)\; public engagement through
  Winter Workspace programming and a Meet the Artist program\; mentorship w
 ith Wave Hill curatorial staff\, working artists and arts professionals\; 
 and AnkhLave Alumni Network benefits. ELIGIBILITY: emerging artists 30 or 
 younger (born 1997 or after) from historically underrepresented communitie
 s\; live in one of the five NYC boroughs\; demonstrate financial need\; ha
 ve completed college and not be enrolled in a degree-granting program duri
 ng the residency\; not represented by a commercial gallery\; available for
  both programs\; cannot have been a Van Lier Fellow elsewhere or have prev
 iously done a Winter Workspace residency or exhibited at Wave Hill or with
  AnkhLave. Works may not include nudity\, depictions of violence or profan
 ity. Artists may apply to only one of the two 2027 AnkhLave Garden Project
  opportunities. Questions: visualarts@wavehill.org with '2027 Van Lier-Ank
 hlave' in the subject. DEADLINE: 10 August 2026. Apply via SlideRoom.\n\nO
 rganisation: Wave Hill / AnkhLave Arts Alliance\nLocation: Wave Hill Publi
 c Garden and Cultural Center\, the Bronx\, New York City\, USA. For NYC-ba
 sed BIPOC visual artists aged 30 or younger.\nAward: $10\,435 stipend\, in
 cluding an $8\,000 honorarium\, a transportation stipend for the residency
 \, and professional development opportunities\, plus the Winter Workspace 
 residency\, a solo exhibition with public programs\, mentorship from Wave 
 Hill curatorial staff and arts professionals\, and AnkhLave Alumni Network
  benefits. Two fellowships awarded. No application fee.\nDuration: January
  to December 2027\; Winter Workspace residency 23 February - 18 April 2027
 \; solo exhibition 15 May - 4 July 2027\n\nMore: https://wavehill.slideroo
 m.com/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral#/login/pr
 ogram/89300
URL:https://wavehill.slideroom.com/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&u
 tm_medium=referral#/login/program/89300
LOCATION:Wave Hill Public Garden and Cultural Center\, the Bronx\, New York
  City\, USA. For NYC-based BIPOC visual artists aged 30 or younger.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:wave-hill-sunroom-project-space-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260831T203817Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260809
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260810
SUMMARY:Deadline: Wave Hill: 2027 Sunroom Project Space (NYC)
DESCRIPTION:The Sunroom Project Space gives artists in the New York City ar
 ea who are in the early stages of their careers\, regardless of age\, the 
 chance to develop and show a site-specific solo project in the Sunroom or 
 Sun Porch of Glyndor Gallery at Wave Hill. For the 2027 season\, Wave Hill
  is especially interested in projects that recognise ancestral wisdom in r
 elation to our connection with the earth and soil: practices\, beliefs and
  values passed down through generations\, particularly those that foster h
 armonious relationships with our ecosystems\, for example regenerative far
 ming and agricultural practices and the care of soil\, water and plant lif
 e. Projects engaging the history of earth or land art (concepts\, material
 s\, sites and relationships to place) that intersect with sustainable prac
 tices and ancestral wisdom are also welcome. AWARD: four artists are selec
 ted for solo presentations\, each receiving a $2\,000 honorarium\, exhibit
 ion and professional development support\, and nine to twelve months to re
 search and develop their ideas. Each project is accompanied by a Meet the 
 Artist program co-designed with the artist\, and a short exhibition essay 
 published in print and online. ELIGIBILITY: artists working across media\,
  in the early stages of their career regardless of education\, living with
 in a 50-mile radius of the Bronx. Not eligible: students enrolled in a deg
 ree-granting program\; artists with commercial gallery representation\; ar
 tists who have previously exhibited a site-specific project at Wave Hill\;
  artists who participated in the 2026 Winter Workspace program at Wave Hil
 l. Applications are reviewed by a jury of Wave Hill's Curator of Visual Ar
 ts\, an invited guest curator and a prior 2026 Sunroom Project Space artis
 t. An online information session is held Monday 13 July\, 12-1PM\; RSVP to
  visualarts@wavehill.org with the subject line '2027 Sunroom Project Space
  Info Session'. DEADLINE: 9 August 2026. Apply via SlideRoom.\n\nOrganisat
 ion: Wave Hill\nLocation: Glyndor Gallery\, Wave Hill\, the Bronx\, New Yo
 rk City\, USA. For early-career artists living within a 50-mile radius of 
 the Bronx.\nAward: $2\,000 honorarium per artist\, plus exhibition and pro
 fessional development support\, a co-designed Meet the Artist public progr
 am\, and a short exhibition essay published in print and online. Four arti
 sts selected. No application fee.\nDuration: Nine to twelve months of rese
 arch and development leading to a solo presentation during the 2027 season
 \n\nMore: https://wavehill.slideroom.com/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugran
 tdesk&utm_medium=referral#/login/program/89416
URL:https://wavehill.slideroom.com/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&u
 tm_medium=referral#/login/program/89416
LOCATION:Glyndor Gallery\, Wave Hill\, the Bronx\, New York City\, USA. For
  early-career artists living within a 50-mile radius of the Bronx.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:mondriaan-fund-delfina-foundation-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.gith
 ub.io
DTSTAMP:20260831T203817Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260827
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260828
SUMMARY:Deadline: Mondriaan Fund: Delfina Foundation Residency 2027 (London
 )
DESCRIPTION:Mondriaan Fund-supported working period at London's Delfina Fou
 ndation\, one of the UK's best known artist-in-residence programmes\, hous
 ed at 29-31 Catherine Place near Buckingham Palace with space for 6 to 8 i
 nternational residents (own room\, shared kitchen and facilities). Delfina
  promotes artistic exchange and experiment\, offering visual artists and c
 urators a platform to carry out research\, develop ideas and position thei
 r practice within the global discourse\, with introductions to the London 
 art scene and Delfina's international network. The programme includes visi
 ts to museums\, galleries and non-profit platforms\, discussions with Lond
 on-based artists\, portfolio reviews with curators and regular networking 
 lunches\; residents are expected to take part. Applicants are not asked fo
 r a concrete project proposal but must submit a clear motivation: why they
  wish to take part\, what research they want to conduct\, and how it can c
 ontribute to Delfina's ongoing programme. WHO: visual artists and curators
  based in the Netherlands or the Caribbean part of the Kingdom\; duo appli
 cations not possible\; application must be in English. One work period ava
 ilable: 27 September to 17 December 2027. Selection by an advisory committ
 ee with a Delfina representative\; processing may exceed three months. DEA
 DLINE: Thursday 27 August 2026\, before 16:00 Dutch time / 11:00 Caribbean
  time.\n\nOrganisation: Mondriaan Fund / Delfina Foundation\nLocation: Lon
 don\, UK. For visual artists and curators based in the Netherlands or the 
 Caribbean part of the Kingdom\, funded by the Mondriaan Fund.\nAward: Subs
 idy of EUR 9\,188 for an artist or EUR 7\,232 for a curator/art observer t
 oward travel\, material and living costs (a 10 percent personal contributi
 on is automatically deducted by the Mondriaan Fund)\; studio\, living spac
 e and Delfina Foundation support are paid directly by the Mondriaan Fund. 
 Contribution for Caribbean-based artists can be increased for higher trave
 l costs. No application fee.\nDuration: Three months: 27 September to 17 D
 ecember 2027\n\nMore: https://www.mondriaanfonds.nl/en/apply-for-a-grant/g
 rants/residency/delfina-foundation-londen-uk/?utm_source=artificialnouveau
 grantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.mondriaanfonds.nl/en/apply-for-a-grant/grants/residency/del
 fina-foundation-londen-uk/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_mediu
 m=referral
LOCATION:London\, UK. For visual artists and curators based in the Netherla
 nds or the Caribbean part of the Kingdom\, funded by the Mondriaan Fund.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:mondriaan-fund-inside-out-art-museum-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.g
 ithub.io
DTSTAMP:20260831T203817Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260827
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260828
SUMMARY:Deadline: Mondriaan Fund: Inside-Out Art Museum Residency 2027 (Bei
 jing)
DESCRIPTION:Mondriaan Fund-supported working period at Inside-Out Art Museu
 m (IOAM) in Beijing\, one of China's leading independent platforms for con
 temporary art and research. The museum combines exhibitions\, critical inq
 uiry and public programmes\, giving residents room for in-depth research\,
  experimentation and exchange within a Chinese art scene that is otherwise
  hard to access from Europe. The residency is framed as cultural exchange 
 rather than production to deadline: IOAM works with a flexible model that 
 takes the resident's other obligations into account and sets the exact sta
 rt date in consultation with the selected candidate. WHO: visual artists\,
  curators and critics based in the Netherlands or the Caribbean part of th
 e Kingdom. Duos and collaborations may apply (two artists\, two curators/c
 ritics\, or a combination who structurally make work together\, submitting
  a joint plan for the work period that leads to a single result\, and who 
 live and work together in the same space during the residency)\, but each 
 individual must submit a separate application\; the apartment is well suit
 ed to duos or partnerships. WORK PERIOD: one period of three months\, 1 Ma
 rch to 30 May 2027\, with room for one artist or duo\; you can state a pre
 ference for the work period in the application form. Selection is by advis
 ory committee\; read the Mondriaan Fund Residency explanation for the cond
 itions\, assessment and checklist\, plus the fund's general terms and cond
 itions\, before applying. DEADLINE: Thursday 27 August 2026\, before 16:00
  Dutch time / 10:00 Caribbean time.\n\nOrganisation: Mondriaan Fund / Insi
 de-Out Art Museum\nLocation: Beijing\, China. For visual artists\, curator
 s and critics based in the Netherlands or the Caribbean part of the Kingdo
 m\, funded by the Mondriaan Fund.\nAward: Subsidy of EUR 8\,478 for an art
 ist or EUR 5\,622 for a curator/critic toward travel\, material and living
  costs (a 10 percent personal contribution is automatically deducted by th
 e Mondriaan Fund)\; studio\, living space and Inside-Out Art Museum suppor
 t are paid directly by the Mondriaan Fund. For a selected duo the total is
  increased proportionally to cover the second applicant's travel and accom
 modation. Contribution for Caribbean-based residents can be increased for 
 higher travel costs. No application fee.\nDuration: Three months: 1 March 
 to 30 May 2027 (flexible start date\, set by IOAM in consultation with the
  resident)\n\nMore: https://www.mondriaanfonds.nl/subsidie-aanvragen/regel
 ingen/residency/inside-out-art-museum-beijing-china/?utm_source=artificial
 nouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.mondriaanfonds.nl/subsidie-aanvragen/regelingen/residency/i
 nside-out-art-museum-beijing-china/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&
 utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Beijing\, China. For visual artists\, curators and critics based i
 n the Netherlands or the Caribbean part of the Kingdom\, funded by the Mon
 driaan Fund.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:james-castle-house-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260831T203817Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260828
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260829
SUMMARY:Deadline: James Castle House: 2027 Artist Residencies (Boise\, Idah
 o)
DESCRIPTION:The James Castle House in Boise\, Idaho (the preserved home of 
 self-taught artist James Castle) opens applications for its 2027 residency
  terms from 16 July to 28 August 2026. TWO-MONTH RESIDENCY: an immersive f
 ocus on a project or body of work responding to the history and legacy of 
 James Castle or the site\; open to artists\, scholars\, creators and profe
 ssionals in any field\; $4\,000 stipend\; residents share their practice t
 hrough public events (workshops\, open studios\, presentations) and donate
  a selected piece to the City of Boise collection. Terms: 1 March - 30 Apr
 il\, 1 June - 31 July\, or 1 September - 31 October 2027. TWO-WEEK RESIDEN
 CY: time and space for a single site-responsive project\; $1\,000 stipend\
 ; one public event. Terms: 11-25 January or 1-15 December 2027. A rolling 
 PROJECT RESIDENCY also considers proposals case by case (email jamescastle
 house@cityofboise.org). ELIGIBILITY: 18+\, legally able to work in the Uni
 ted States\, able to pass a background check\; emerging and mid-career pra
 ctitioners in any field\, though the property cannot accommodate loud or e
 specially messy processes. Residents live alone on site. Selection by comm
 ittee on strength of proposal\, application\, work samples and references.
  Virtual information session 21 July 2026\, 1pm MT. Applicants notified Se
 ptember 2026. DEADLINE: 28 August 2026.\n\nOrganisation: James Castle Hous
 e / City of Boise\nLocation: Boise\, Idaho\, USA. Open to applicants legal
 ly able to work in the United States.\nAward: $4\,000 stipend for two-mont
 h terms or $1\,000 for two-week terms\, to assist with living expenses and
  supplies\, plus solo live-in accommodation and studio at the historic Jam
 es Castle House. Residents donate one selected piece to the City of Boise 
 collection at the end of the term. No application fee.\nDuration: Two-mont
 h terms (1 Mar - 30 Apr\, 1 Jun - 31 Jul\, 1 Sep - 31 Oct 2027) or two-wee
 k terms (11-25 Jan and 1-15 Dec 2027)\n\nMore: https://www.jamescastlehous
 e.org/residencies/apply/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=
 referral
