DTSTAMP:20260831T203817Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260721
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260722
SUMMARY:Deadline: VH AWARD 2026 (Hyundai Motor Group)
DESCRIPTION:The VH AWARD\, hosted by Hyundai Motor Group\, supports emergin
 g media artists whose work engages with the context of Asia\, through an o
 nline residency and exhibitions across global platforms. FIELD: audiovisua
 l\, screen-based artworks including video art\, motion graphics\, animatio
 n\, games\, films or newly explored areas\; proposals must suit single-cha
 nnel video presentation (no interactivity). ELIGIBILITY: individuals or co
 llectives whose work engages with the context of Asia\, including artists 
 of Asian descent\, those based in Asia\, and the Asian diaspora. Five fina
 lists are selected\, each receiving a USD 30\,000 production grant and a p
 lace in the Ars Electronica online residency program (masterclasses and 1:
 1 mentoring)\, with networking and exhibition opportunities\; one Grand Pr
 ix recipient (announced 2027) receives an additional USD 30\,000\; a new H
 onorary Mention category recognises one or two further applicants with web
 site features and selected residency components. APPLY: via the VH AWARD w
 ebsite Entry Portal with a video portfolio (max 3 min)\, CV and artist sta
 tement (max 3 pages)\, and a new artwork proposal (max 3 pages) with a ref
 erence video (max 1 min)\; all documents in English\; proposed works must 
 be original and unexhibited. Open call 26 May - 21 July 2026 (KST)\; final
 ists announced September 2026.\n\nOrganisation: Hyundai Motor Group\nLocat
 ion: Online residency (global exhibitions)\; for artists engaging with Asi
 a\nAward: Each of five finalists receives a USD 30\,000 production grant p
 lus an Ars Electronica online residency\; the Grand Prix winner receives a
 n additional USD 30\,000 (USD 60\,000 total). Honorary Mentions join selec
 ted residency components. No application fee.\nDuration: Online residency 
 Sep 2026 - Mar 2027 (finalists)\; award ceremony and exhibitions June 2027
 \n\nMore: https://vhaward.com/about/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk
 &utm_medium=referral#entry
URL:https://vhaward.com/about/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_me
 dium=referral#entry
LOCATION:Online residency (global exhibitions)\; for artists engaging with 
 Asia
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stichting-stokroos-maker-initiatives-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260831T203817Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260731
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260801
SUMMARY:Deadline: Stichting Stokroos: Maker Initiatives Grant 2026
DESCRIPTION:Stichting Stokroos Maker Initiatives supports established visua
 l artists\, designers and craft practitioners (overlap possible)\, includi
 ng duos and collectives\, in developing and realising a multivocal artisti
 c project or programme centred on a common concern\, in collaboration with
  other makers or communities. There is one application round per year and 
 Stokroos can support 4 to 6 proposals\; a maximum of 40 eligible applicati
 ons are considered per period. Eligibility: you completed your first subje
 ct-specific (vocational or higher) programme in 2020 or earlier\, or have 
 an equivalent established track record\, or started without formal trainin
 g (first presentation marks the start of your practice)\; at least 21 year
 s old\; living and working in the Kingdom of the Netherlands (including it
 s Caribbean parts) or Suriname for at least one year\; not currently enrol
 led in a study or post-academic programme. You must apply together with an
  artistic or creative partner (from professional makers to communities)\; 
 duos and collectives must also have an external partner. You may submit on
 ly one application per year across all Stokroos grants\, and must not have
  received a Seed Grant rejection in the previous calendar year. The grant 
 is a fixed contribution of EUR 25\,000 or EUR 40\,000 depending on need. P
 lans can take place anywhere\, start in the next calendar year and last a 
 maximum of two years. Applications are submitted via the online form in Du
 tch or English (portfolio PDF up to 20 pages/person\, optional video up to
  10 minutes total\, CV up to 2 pages/person\, budget up to 3 pages\, work/
 plan/collaboration descriptions up to 2\,500 characters each). Stokroos ai
 ms to respond within 10 weeks\; no appeal is possible. Application window:
  20 to 31 July 2026. Questions: mail@stokroos.nl.\n\nOrganisation: Stichti
 ng Stokroos\nLocation: Kingdom of the Netherlands (including its Caribbean
  parts) or Suriname\; must have lived and worked there at least one year. 
 Applicants outside the Randstad\, or plans taking place there\, are partic
 ularly encouraged.\nAward: Fixed grant of EUR 25\,000 or EUR 40\,000 (chos
 en depending on need). Maximum participant fee EUR 2\,200/month (40-hour w
 eek)\; third-party hire capped at EUR 85/hour excl. VAT. Co-funding not re
 quired. No application fee.\nDuration: Plan starts in the next calendar ye
 ar (2027) and runs a maximum of two years.\n\nMore: https://stokroos.nl/en
 /grant-rules/guidelines-maker-initiatives/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugra
 ntdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://stokroos.nl/en/grant-rules/guidelines-maker-initiatives/?utm_so
 urce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Kingdom of the Netherlands (including its Caribbean parts) or Suri
 name\; must have lived and worked there at least one year. Applicants outs
 ide the Randstad\, or plans taking place there\, are particularly encourag
 ed.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stichting-stokroos-residency-fundaziun-nairs-2026@artificialnouveau.git
 hub.io
DTSTAMP:20260831T203817Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260911
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260912
SUMMARY:Deadline: Stichting Stokroos: Residency at Fundaziun Nairs 2026
DESCRIPTION:Stichting Stokroos funds a three-month reflective residency at 
 Fundaziun Nairs in Scuol\, Switzerland\, for one selected visual artist\, 
 designer or craft practitioner (overlap possible). Both emerging and estab
 lished makers may apply. Stokroos covers full accommodation and meals dire
 ctly with Fundaziun Nairs and provides a discretionary EUR 7\,000 budget f
 or living\, travel and production. The application should include a propos
 al that engages specifically with the residency\, its Alpine surroundings 
 and/or its historical and cultural context. Eligibility: you completed you
 r first subject-specific (vocational or higher) programme in 2022 or earli
 er\, or have an equivalent established practice\, or started without forma
 l training (first presentation marks the start of your practice)\; at leas
 t 21 years old\; living and working in the Kingdom of the Netherlands (inc
 luding its Caribbean parts) or Suriname for at least one year\; not curren
 tly enrolled in a study or post-academic programme. Applications are indiv
 idual only\; duos and collectives cannot apply. Makers already selected by
  Fundaziun Nairs may still apply if they meet the criteria. You may submit
  only one application per year across all Stokroos grants\, and must not h
 ave received a Seed Grant rejection in the previous calendar year. Apply v
 ia the online form (Dutch or English) with a portfolio PDF up to 20 pages\
 , optional video up to 10 minutes total\, CV up to 2 pages\, and work/plan
  descriptions up to 2\,500 characters each. Selection includes an introduc
 tory interview with up to three candidates\; Stokroos aims to respond with
 in 8 weeks. No appeal is possible. Application window: 1 to 11 September 2
 026. More information at nairs.ch.\n\nOrganisation: Stichting Stokroos\nLo
 cation: Residency in Scuol\, Switzerland (Fundaziun Nairs). Applicants mus
 t live and work in the Kingdom of the Netherlands (including its Caribbean
  parts) or Suriname for at least one year. Applicants outside the Randstad
  particularly encouraged.\nAward: Fully supported stay (accommodation and 
 meals paid directly to Fundaziun Nairs) plus an unrestricted living\, trav
 el and production budget of EUR 7\,000. 80% paid before the residency\, th
 e remainder on receipt of a brief final report. No application fee.\nDurat
 ion: Intensive three-month working period (July through September).\n\nMor
 e: https://stokroos.nl/en/grant-rules/guidelines-residency-fundaziun-nairs
 /?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://stokroos.nl/en/grant-rules/guidelines-residency-fundaziun-nairs
 /?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Residency in Scuol\, Switzerland (Fundaziun Nairs). Applicants mus
 t live and work in the Kingdom of the Netherlands (including its Caribbean
  parts) or Suriname for at least one year. Applicants outside the Randstad
  particularly encouraged.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stichting-stokroos-seed-grant-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260831T203817Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261031
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261101
SUMMARY:Deadline: Stichting Stokroos: Seed Grant 2026
DESCRIPTION:The Stichting Stokroos Seed Grant gives individual makers\, duo
 s and collectives time and space to focus on their artistic development\, 
 for example a focused working period for research and experiment\, or the 
 development of a prototype\, new work or methodology. There are two applic
 ation rounds in 2026: 15 May to 30 June 2026 (now full) and 1 September to
  31 October 2026\; Stokroos considers a maximum of 60 eligible application
 s per period (or closes once the budget is reached) and supports around 50
  applications per year. Eligibility: active as a visual artist\, designer 
 and/or craft practitioner (overlap possible)\; living and working in the K
 ingdom of the Netherlands (including its Caribbean parts) or Suriname for 
 at least one year\; at least 21 years old\; you completed your first subje
 ct-specific (vocational or higher) programme between 2018 and 2022\, or st
 arted without formal training (first presentation marks the start of your 
 practice)\; not currently enrolled in a study or post-academic programme. 
 Duos and collectives may apply provided all participants meet the guidelin
 es. The grant is a fixed amount with no budget required: EUR 5\,000 (indiv
 idual)\, EUR 7\,500 (duo) or EUR 10\,000 (collective). Plans can take plac
 e anywhere\, start at least 10 weeks after submission and last a maximum o
 f one year. You may apply for the Seed Grant once every two calendar years
  and receive it up to twice\, and may submit only one application per year
  across all Stokroos grants. Apply via the online form (Dutch or English) 
 with a portfolio PDF up to 20 pages/person\, optional video up to 10 minut
 es total\, CV up to 2 pages/person\, and work/plan/collaboration descripti
 ons up to 2\,500 characters each. Stokroos aims to respond within 8 weeks\
 ; no appeal is possible. Next deadline: 31 October 2026.\n\nOrganisation: 
 Stichting Stokroos\nLocation: Kingdom of the Netherlands (including its Ca
 ribbean parts) or Suriname\; must have lived and worked there at least one
  year. Applicants outside the Randstad\, or plans taking place there\, par
 ticularly encouraged.\nAward: Fixed grant (no project budget required): EU
