SUMMARY:Deadline: Flickr x Black Women Photographers Grant 2026 (Traces of 
 Connection)
DESCRIPTION:Flickr and Black Women Photographers award a USD 10\,000 grant 
 to a Black female or non-binary photographer to invest in their practice. 
 The 2026 edition centers on the theme Traces of Connection\, chosen by 202
 5 recipient and guest judge Eleonore Menga. TO APPLY: be a member of the B
 lack Women Photographers organization (free)\, join the BWP Flickr Communi
 ty\, submit one photograph inspired by the theme to the community\, and sh
 are a brief description of how the image connects to it. The winner also r
 eceives a two-year Flickr Pro and a one-year SmugMug Pro membership\, and 
 is announced live at the first MODE by Flickr festival in Minneapolis (18-
 20 September 2026)\; ten additional recipients receive Flickr Pro and Smug
 Mug Pro memberships. DEADLINE: 6 August 2026. No entry fee.\n\nOrganisatio
 n: Flickr and Black Women Photographers (BWP)\nLocation: Open internationa
 lly to Black female and non-binary photographers\; winner announced at the
  MODE by Flickr festival in Minneapolis\, USA (18-20 September 2026).\nAwa
 rd: USD 10\,000 grant to invest in the recipient's practice\, plus a two-y
 ear Flickr Pro and one-year SmugMug Pro membership\; ten additional recipi
 ents each receive one-year Flickr Pro and SmugMug Pro memberships. No entr
 y fee (BWP membership is free).\nDuration: Winner announced live at MODE b
 y Flickr\, 18-20 September 2026\n\nMore: https://blackwomenphotographers.c
 om/smugmug-flickr?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referra
 l
URL:https://blackwomenphotographers.com/smugmug-flickr?utm_source=artificia
 lnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Open internationally to Black female and non-binary photographers\
 ; winner announced at the MODE by Flickr festival in Minneapolis\, USA (18
 -20 September 2026).
END:VEVENT
