UID:apostaxis-residency-exhibition-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260831T203817Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260726
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260727
SUMMARY:Deadline: APOSTAXIS Artist Residency & Exhibition 2026 (Ukraine / C
 yprus)
DESCRIPTION:APOSTAXIS is an international residency and exhibition programm
 e exploring displacement\, memory\, identity and cultural resilience. It s
 elects four visual artists (three from Ukraine and one from Cyprus) for tw
 o simultaneous 20-day residencies in Ternopil\, Ukraine and Larnaca\, Cypr
 us (6 to 28 October 2026)\, followed by post-production\, a digital exhibi
 tion\, and a curated physical exhibition in Larnaca in January 2027. ELIGI
 BILITY: visual artists from Ukraine and Cyprus with lived experience or fa
 mily heritage connected to displacement\, working in community-engaged or 
 research-based practices (installation\, mixed media\, participatory\, soc
 ial practice\, documentary\, performance\, archive-based work). Artists un
 able to travel due to war-related restrictions or personal circumstances r
 emain eligible via hybrid participation. Fully funded: EUR 1\,800 artist f
 ee (equivalent UAH for Ukrainian artists)\, EUR 300 production budget\, tr
 avel\, accommodation\, meals and curatorial support\; no application fee. 
 Deadline: 26 July 2026.\n\nOrganisation: ZMINA (Ukraine) with Cypriot part
 ner organisation\nLocation: Ternopil\, Ukraine and Larnaca\, Cyprus (hybri
 d participation possible)\nAward: Fully funded: artist fee of EUR 1\,800 (
 including tax\; paid in equivalent UAH for Ukrainian artists)\, EUR 300 pr
 oduction budget\, plus travel\, accommodation\, meals and curatorial suppo
 rt. No application fee.\nDuration: 20-day residency\, 6 to 28 October 2026
 \, with a group exhibition in Larnaca in January 2027\n\nMore: https://art
 infoland.com/opportunities/apostaxis-artist-residency-2026-ukraine-cyprus?
 utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://artinfoland.com/opportunities/apostaxis-artist-residency-2026-u
 kraine-cyprus?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Ternopil\, Ukraine and Larnaca\, Cyprus (hybrid participation poss
 ible)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:transmediale-pro-helvetia-digital-art-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.
 github.io
DTSTAMP:20260831T203817Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260828
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260829
SUMMARY:Deadline: transmediale x Pro Helvetia Digital Art Residency 2027
DESCRIPTION:The fifth iteration of transmediale's Digital Art Residency\, r
 un with the Swiss Arts Council Pro Helvetia\, awarded to one individual or
  collective working in digital art practices at the intersection of media 
 arts\, performance\, sound and moving image. THEME: the 2027 programme sit
 s under transmediale's 40th-anniversary framework RFC 40\, named after the
  early internet Request for Comments series\, and treats the festival as a
  counter-infrastructure: the call asks how a network stays legible to itse
 lf while surrounding structures break down\, and how technical paradigms c
 an be reconfigured into new cultural protocols outside extractive logics\,
  moving from critique to construction. Proposals should offer alternatives
  to how we understand\, respond to and shape the technological conditions 
 we inhabit. WHAT IS OFFERED: an artist fee of CHF 2\,000 per month for two
  months\; a CHF 15\,000 production grant supporting a new work or the cont
 inuation of an existing project\, open to all formats and building on the 
 research begun during the residency (the project must be completed by Dece
 mber 2027 at the latest)\; travel and accommodation for the festival and t
 he residency\; a shared modular working space at transmediale studio\; con
 nections to Berlin institutions and stakeholders\; a public presentation i
 n transmediale's year-round studio programme\; and the option of an online
  publication in transmediale's journal. STRUCTURE: kick-off with a present
 ation of the residency projects during transmediale 2027 (26 to 31 January
  2027\, attendance optional but strongly recommended)\; onboarding and the
  first hybrid stretch in May 2027\; the mandatory on-site month in Berlin 
 in June 2027\; and a second hybrid stretch including reporting in July 202
 7. Availability for the festival week and for the whole of June in Berlin 
 are treated as key prerequisites. TIMELINE: open call 16 July to 28 August
  2026 (23:59 CEST)\; selected residents announced October 2026. Applicatio
 ns are only accepted via transmediale's submission forms. Contact: info[at
 ]transmediale.de.\n\nOrganisation: transmediale (in cooperation with the S
 wiss Arts Council Pro Helvetia)\nLocation: Hybrid: remote plus on-site at 
 transmediale studio\, silent green Kulturquartier\, Berlin-Wedding\, Germa
 ny. RESTRICTED: applicants must hold Swiss nationality or permanent reside
 nce in Switzerland and be firmly established in the Swiss cultural scene (
 Pro Helvetia's general requirements apply).\nAward: Artist fee of CHF 2\,0
 00 per month across the two-month residency (CHF 4\,000)\, plus a producti
 on grant of CHF 15\,000 for the selected project\, plus travel and accommo
 dation for both the festival and the residency month. Duos and collectives
  may apply but the fee and the production grant stay the same and must be 
 shared. No application fee.\nDuration: Two-month hybrid residency between 
 mid-May and mid-July 2027\, with the whole of June 2027 on-site in Berlin 
 (mandatory)\n\nMore: https://transmediale.de/en/news/digital-art-residency
 -2027?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://transmediale.de/en/news/digital-art-residency-2027?utm_source=a
 rtificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Hybrid: remote plus on-site at transmediale studio\, silent green 
 Kulturquartier\, Berlin-Wedding\, Germany. RESTRICTED: applicants must hol
 d Swiss nationality or permanent residence in Switzerland and be firmly es
 tablished in the Swiss cultural scene (Pro Helvetia's general requirements
  apply).
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:moorhead-call-public-art-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260831T203817Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260904
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260905
SUMMARY:Deadline: City of Moorhead: 2026 Call for Public Art (Movable Inter
 active Piece)
DESCRIPTION:The City of Moorhead is seeking proposals for an inspirational\
 , movable public artwork to be installed at rotating locations across the 
 city. Interactive elements are explicitly encouraged\, with kinetic sculpt
 ure\, digital installation and tactile elements named as examples. Strong 
 proposals invite public participation\, promote creativity and youth engag
 ement\, are safe for all members of the public\, are durable enough for ye
 ar-round outdoor conditions\, and draw people to gather. Submissions are r
 eviewed and ranked by the Artist Review Team\, whose recommendation passes
  to the Art and Culture Commission and then to City Council for the final 
 decision. Questions go to art@moorheadmn.gov. Proposals are due by 10:00am
  on Friday 4 September 2026.\n\nOrganisation: City of Moorhead\, Minnesota
 \nLocation: Moorhead\, Minnesota\, USA. The piece will be sited at differe
 nt locations throughout the city. No geographic eligibility restriction is
  stated in the call\, so non-US artists appear eligible\, but this is not 
 confirmed in writing.\nAward: Not published. The call announcement states 
 no budget\, commission amount or artist fee\, and the linked Request for A
 rt document could not be retrieved. Confirm the budget with art@moorheadmn
 .gov before investing time in a proposal. No application fee is mentioned.
 \nDuration: Single commission\; timeline not published\n\nMore: https://ww
 w.moorheadmn.gov/news/posts/2026-call-for-public-art/?utm_source=artificia
 lnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.moorheadmn.gov/news/posts/2026-call-for-public-art/?utm_sou
 rce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Moorhead\, Minnesota\, USA. The piece will be sited at different l
 ocations throughout the city. No geographic eligibility restriction is sta
 ted in the call\, so non-US artists appear eligible\, but this is not conf
 irmed in writing.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:penn-college-gallery-exhibitions-2027-28@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260831T203817Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260831
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260901
SUMMARY:Deadline: The Gallery at Penn College: 2027-28 Call for Exhibitions
DESCRIPTION:The Gallery at Penn College is accepting proposals for solo\, t
 wo-person and group exhibitions in its 2027-28 season. All entries are jur
 ied through a blind selection process by a gallery committee of faculty\, 
 staff\, K-12 art educators and community artists. The space is 3\,000 squa
 re feet with 82 to 250 running feet of linear wall depending on configurat
 ion and a ceiling height of 11 feet 4 inches\, and all exhibitions are ins
 talled by gallery staff. Site-specific installations requiring artist inst
 allation need an approved planning document first. Campus visits are a val
 ued part of programming though some exhibitions are scheduled without one\
 ; visiting artists give a 20 to 30 minute gallery talk at the public recep
 tion\, and are encouraged to propose class-specific programmes or communit
 y workshops. Promotional support includes an annual gallery catalogue\, po
 stcards\, press releases and web and social coverage. Applications require
  10 to 15 digital images (JPG only\, max 4 MB each)\, an image list with d
 imensions and medium\, a CV and an artist statement.\n\nOrganisation: The 
 Gallery at Penn College (Pennsylvania College of Technology)\nLocation: Wi
 lliamsport\, Pennsylvania\, USA\, on the Pennsylvania College of Technolog
 y campus. Travel note: Williamsport Regional Airport connects only to Wash
 ington Dulles\, with no other direct flights or trains\, so international 
 travel involves a connection. No nationality restriction is stated.\nAward
 : Housing\, meals\, a solo exhibition honorarium\, and a shipping and trav
 el stipend are all provided. Specific figures are not published in the cal
 l. No application fee is stated.\nDuration: Exhibition slot within the 202
 7-28 season\; review takes place during autumn semester with artists notif
 ied in January\n\nMore: https://www.pct.edu/gallery/exhibitions-entry-form
 ?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.pct.edu/gallery/exhibitions-entry-form?utm_source=artificia
 lnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Williamsport\, Pennsylvania\, USA\, on the Pennsylvania College of
  Technology campus. Travel note: Williamsport Regional Airport connects on
 ly to Washington Dulles\, with no other direct flights or trains\, so inte
 rnational travel involves a connection. No nationality restriction is stat
 ed.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:art-explora-cite-internationale-des-arts-2027@artificialnouveau.github.
 io
DTSTAMP:20260831T203817Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261106
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261107
SUMMARY:Deadline: Art Explora x Cite internationale des arts Residency Prog
 ramme\, 2027 Sessions
DESCRIPTION:Residency programme run by the Art Explora Foundation with the 
 Cite internationale des arts at its Montmartre site\, supporting work that
  engages scientific and technological exploration and the major social and
  environmental issues of the present. Residents receive a studio-apartment
  of around 50 sqm\, a monthly living grant of EUR 1\,000\, a production gr
 ant of up to EUR 3\,000\, and a round-trip travel grant\, plus access to p
 roduction facilities and local networks. Two tracks are offered: a SOLO pr
 ogramme for artists and writers across visual arts\, performance\, digital
  practices\, literary and other experimental disciplines\, and a COLLECTIV
 E programme for duos or collectives working collaboratively on interdiscip
 linary\, experimental or research-based projects\, for which a single stud
 io-apartment designed for collaborative work hosts two residents sharing a
  bed\, and only one member should submit the application. Eligible artisti
 c disciplines are visual arts\, performance and live arts\, digital arts\,
  curatorial practices\, and writing and literary practices\; eligible rese
 arch fields are humanities\, social sciences\, cultural studies and histor
 y\, technological innovation\, and ecology. No output is required at the e
 nd of the residency\, but participation in the Open Studios is mandatory. 
 ELIGIBILITY: artists\, artist collectives\, researchers\, curators and wri
 ters of all nationalities\, no age restriction\, with a minimum of five ye
 ars of professional activity and works or research exhibited at national o
 r international level. The Cite lists 20 to 22 residencies per year on thi
 s programme. Deadline 6 November 2026\, 23:59 Europe/Paris. Questions: res
 idences@artexplora.org. FLAG: the grant figures above come from the open-c
 all text supplied to the desk\; neither the Cite nor Art Explora publishes
  amounts on the programme page\, so confirm them\, along with the exact de
 adline\, before applying.\n\nOrganisation: Art Explora Foundation with the
  Cite internationale des arts\nLocation: Paris\, France (Cite internationa
 le des arts\, Montmartre site\, 24 rue Norvins\, 75018). Open to applicant
 s of all nationalities with no age restriction.\nAward: Monthly living gra
 nt of EUR 1\,000\, production grant of up to EUR 3\,000\, a round-trip tra
 vel grant\, and a fully equipped studio-apartment of roughly 50 sqm. For c
 ollectives and duos the living grant (up to EUR 2\,000) and the production
  grant (up to EUR 3\,000) are shared between members. Access to production
  facilities and local networks. No application fee.\nDuration: 3 to 6 mont
 hs. Session 1: March to August 2027. Session 2: September 2027 to February
  2028.\n\nMore: https://www.citeinternationaledesarts.fr/en/programme-de-r
 esidence/art-explora-x-cite-internationale-des-arts/?utm_source=artificial
 nouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.citeinternationaledesarts.fr/en/programme-de-residence/art-
 explora-x-cite-internationale-des-arts/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantd
 esk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Paris\, France (Cite internationale des arts\, Montmartre site\, 2
 4 rue Norvins\, 75018). Open to applicants of all nationalities with no ag
 e restriction.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:helpmann-fellowships-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260831T203817Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260831
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260901
SUMMARY:Deadline: Helpmann Fellowships 2026
DESCRIPTION:Three Helpmann Fellowships of up to AUD 7\,500 support ambitiou
 s\, self-directed projects that advance the artistic and professional deve
 lopment of emerging creatives. Fellowships are open across all eligible di
 sciplines\, to individuals and to collectives\, and funding can go to larg
 er-scale creative projects\, tailored professional development\, or a comb
 ination of both. Previous fellowships have supported the creation of new w
 ork\, exhibitions and performances\, residencies and internships\, touring
  and recording\, specialised training\, and long-term professional develop
 ment\; each fellowship is shaped by the recipient rather than a fixed prog
 ramme. ELIGIBILITY IS NARROW AND GEOGRAPHIC: applicants must be current re
 sidents of South Australia and either final-year students or graduates wit
 hin five years of a supported degree at Adelaide University\, the Universi
 ty of Adelaide\, Flinders University\, or the University of South Australi
 a. Honours students and graduates (up to five years after the final year o
 f study) are eligible where honours was undertaken directly following the 
 undergraduate degree. Masters and PhD candidates and graduates are not eli
 gible unless they qualify through their undergraduate or honours study. Fi
 nal-year students may apply provided the funded activity takes place after
  studies are completed and within the activity timeframe. Applications are
  assessed on artistic merit\, alignment with career development\, feasibil
 ity\, commitment to learning\, and level of ambition. The online applicati
 on requires a CV (max two pages)\, an official academic transcript\, a bud
 get on the Helpmann template\, a timeline\, project confirmations\, letter
 s of support from an academic and an industry referee\, and four to six im
 ages or one to two audio-visual work samples. An online information sessio
 n runs 4 August 2026 at 6pm ACST\, and the Program Manager\, Toni Wills\, 
 takes online or in-person application chats (info@helpmannacademy.com.au).
  Applications opened 15 July 2026 and close 31 August 2026 at 11:59pm ACST
 \, for activity occurring 1 January to 31 December 2027. Free to apply.\n\
 nOrganisation: Helpmann Academy\nLocation: South Australia (applicant must
  be a current South Australian resident)\; funded activity may take place 
 anywhere.\nAward: Up to AUD 7\,500 per fellowship\, three fellowships avai
 lable. Supported by the James & Diana Ramsay Foundation. No application fe
 e.\nDuration: Funded activity must occur between 1 January 2027 and 31 Dec
 ember 2027\n\nMore: https://helpmannacademy.com.au/helpmann-fellowships/?u
 tm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://helpmannacademy.com.au/helpmann-fellowships/?utm_source=artific
 ialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:South Australia (applicant must be a current South Australian resi
 dent)\; funded activity may take place anywhere.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:vbkoe-refusing-rehearsing-resisting-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260831T203817Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260910
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260911
SUMMARY:Deadline: Refusing Rehearsing Resisting: VBKÖ Annual Programme Ope
 n Call 2027-2028
DESCRIPTION:VBKÖ\, the Austrian Association of Wom*n Artists founded in 19
 10\, invites proposals for its annual programme running March 2027 to Febr
 uary 2028. The call reads the present moment through the resurgence of aut
 horitarianism\, fascism\, militarisation\, colonial violence and extractiv
 e capitalism\, and the parallel privatisation of care and criminalisation 
 of solidarity. Drawing on María Galindo's framing of feminism as a projec
 t of social transformation and Sara Ahmed's account of feminist work begin
 ning with refusal\, the programme treats alternative ways of living as som
 ething rehearsed collectively through organising\, creating\, caring\, lis
 tening\, remembering and struggling. VBKÖ seeks a programme of practices 
 that nurture communal care and build a platform for collective rehearsals:
  proposals that allow for tenderness\, that are not afraid of ugly feeling
 s and different truths\, and that explore how contemporary queer and femin
 ist perspectives resonate across artistic\, social and political movements
 . FORMAT REQUIREMENT: only exhibition formats bringing together multiple a
 rtists\, collectives or collaborative practices are accepted. Solo exhibit
 ions\, individual presentations and projects centred on a single artist's 
 work are explicitly not supported. Proposals that activate the exhibition 
 through public programming (screenings\, performances\, workshops\, lectur
 es and other events) are encouraged. Regular opening hours are Fridays and
  Saturdays 2pm to 6pm\; any additional hours must be arranged and staffed 
 by the selected group. The association acknowledges that its own history i
 s marked by violence\, exclusion and discrimination on the basis of religi
 on\, class\, gender\, sexuality and ethnicity\, and states that it activel
 y opposes all forms of discrimination including trans-exclusionary radical
  feminism. APPLICATION: a single PDF (max 5MB) with a programme descriptio
 n (max 2 pages\, images welcome\, English or German\, including preferred 
 dates and duration)\, a CV and biography for every participant (max 1 page
  each)\, a financial plan (Fair Pay encouraged)\, technical requirements\,
  and contact details including email\, mobile number and main residence\; 
 three high-resolution images of work or exhibition sketches sent within th
 e email or via a download link\, labelled with artist name\, work title\, 
 year and proposal title (video links may be included in the proposal). Sen
 d to opencall@vbkoe.org with the subject line 'Open Call + your proposal t
 itle'. Incomplete applications will not be considered. A shortlist is comp
 iled by the VBKÖ team and final selections are made by the VBKÖ board wi
 th an external jury member experienced in contemporary art\, activism and 
 community building\; shortlisted applicants may be asked to present to the
  jury. Results are announced at the beginning of October 2026. Deadline 10
  September 2026\, 23:59. Free to apply.\n\nOrganisation: VBKÖ (Vereinigun
 g bildender Künstler*innen Österreichs\, Austrian Association of Wom*n A
 rtists)\nLocation: Vienna\, Austria (VBKÖ exhibition spaces and shared ki
 tchen)\nAward: EUR 4\,000 total budget per selected project\, covering bot
 h artist fees and production costs (fees\, materials\, labour\, production
 \, transport and other project expenses). Participants based outside Vienn
 a must include travel\, accommodation and shipping within that budget or s
 ecure external funding\; VBKÖ provides invitation and support letters to 
 help raise additional money. Also provided: the spaces and shared kitchen\
 , graphic design of online promotional material\, press announcements\, ph
 oto documentation\, up to 10 hours of technical setup support\, and techni
 cal equipment. Installation and de-installation are the selected group's r
 esponsibility. No application fee.\nDuration: 4 to 6 weeks\, taking place 
 between March 2027 and February 2028\n\nMore: https://www.vbkoe.org/en/ope
 n-call-refusing-rehearsing-resisting/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdes
 k&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.vbkoe.org/en/open-call-refusing-rehearsing-resisting/?utm_s
 ource=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Vienna\, Austria (VBKÖ exhibition spaces and shared kitchen)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:waag-trust-me-im-an-airtist-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260831T203817Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260930
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261001
SUMMARY:Deadline: Trust me\, I'm an AI/rtist: Open Call for Creative Interv
 entions
DESCRIPTION:Waag Futurelab invites artists\, theatre makers\, choreographer
 s\, dancers\, game designers and other creative practitioners to engage di
 rectly with seven experimental generative AI Enablers being co-created wit
 h technologists and dance\, theatre and gaming professionals. The call is 
 an invitation into the development process: selected artists get access to
  the technologies\, datasets\, interfaces and assumptions that shape these
  systems while they are still being built. Rather than testing whether the
  systems work\, artists are asked to interrogate why they work the way the
 y do\, who they are designed for\, what forms of creativity they enable or
  constrain\, and what assumptions about culture\, intelligence\, authorshi
 p\, labour\, bodies\, audiences and society are embedded in them. Waag is 
 looking for individuals and collectives willing to move beyond adoption in
 to investigation\, and welcomes proposals that are speculative\, critical\
 , poetic\, provocative\, humorous\, performative\, constructive or disrupt
 ive\, including work that challenges\, misuses\, reimagines\, hacks\, subv
 erts or plays with the tools\, exposes hidden biases\, questions environme
 ntal costs\, or imagines alternative technological futures. THE SEVEN AI E
 NABLERS\, each requiring an on-site visit to its technology partner: the G
 eneric Procedural Content Generation Enabler (text-to-3D assets and avatar
 s\, CERTH\, Greece)\; the Data-Driven Cultural Content Adaptation Enabler 
 (audience-aware creative content ideation with ranked candidate ideas\, CE
 RTH\, Greece)\; the Cross-Domain Audience Engagement Analytics Enabler (tu
 rning heterogeneous cultural participation data into interpretable engagem
 ent signals\, The Audience Agency\, Warrington\, UK)\; the Dance Style Ana
 lysis and Generation Enabler (dance video into virtual 3D choreography\, d
 issected into body\, effort\, shape and space components\, Centre of Excel
 lence for Research & Innovation\, Cyprus)\; the Immersive Design Integrati
 on Enabler for Dance & Theatre (NLP-driven XR environments with speech-to-
 3D scene editing\, Cyprus)\; the Music-to-Movement Translation Enabler (au
 dio into a time-aligned feature set spanning genre classification\, emotio
 nal valence-arousal analysis\, rhythm extraction and latent-space projecti
 on\, feeding motion generation\, spatial audio and visual choreography\, A
 ristotle University of Thessaloniki\, Greece)\; and the Adaptive Narrative
  Enabler for Games & Theatre (an evolutionary AI trained on creator-writte
 n story elements that generates infinite story variations\, explicitly rej
 ecting LLMs because of their dependence on copyrighted or public-domain co
 rpora that encode 19th and early 20th century sexism\, racism and imperial
 ism\, CAUSA Creation\, Austria). ELIGIBILITY: artists\, designers\, creati
 ve technologists\, theatre makers\, dancers\, choreographers and game desi
 gners\, as individuals or collectives\; applicants must hold a European VA
 T number. An info session with live demonstrations of the AI Enablers runs
  31 July 2026\, 10:00 to 11:30 CEST (meeting ID 995 7016 2341). Applicatio
 ns go through Homerun using the official Application Template\, uploaded a
 s a PDF\; read the Guide for Applicants\, which contains the full Enabler 
 descriptions\, before applying. Questions: zoenie at waag dot org. The AI 
 Enablers and this call are part of the Horizon Europe project HAMLET\, whi
 ch aims to make generative AI accessible to cultural organisations of all 
 sizes. Closes 30 September 2026\, 23:59 CEST. Free to apply.\n\nOrganisati
 on: Waag Futurelab (Horizon Europe project HAMLET)\nLocation: Europe. Enga
 ging with a specific AI Enabler includes an on-site visit to its technolog
 y partner: CERTH (Greece)\, The Audience Agency (Warrington\, UK)\, the Ce
 ntre of Excellence for Research & Innovation (Cyprus)\, Aristotle Universi
 ty of Thessaloniki (Greece)\, or CAUSA Creation (Austria). Final presentat
 ions September 2027.\nAward: EUR 20\,000 commission fee excluding VAT\, in
 clusive of artist fee\, travel\, accommodation and production costs. Appli
 cants must have a VAT number in Europe. No application fee.\nDuration: Jan
 uary to September 2027\, with final presentations in September 2027\n\nMor
 e: https://waag.org/en/article/open-call-creative-interventions-trust-me-i
 m-airtist/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://waag.org/en/article/open-call-creative-interventions-trust-me-i
 m-airtist/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Europe. Engaging with a specific AI Enabler includes an on-site vi
 sit to its technology partner: CERTH (Greece)\, The Audience Agency (Warri
 ngton\, UK)\, the Centre of Excellence for Research & Innovation (Cyprus)\
 , Aristotle University of Thessaloniki (Greece)\, or CAUSA Creation (Austr
 ia). Final presentations September 2027.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:rug-lecturer-arts-culture-media-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260831T203817Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260815
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260816
SUMMARY:Deadline: University of Groningen: Lecturer 4\, Arts\, Culture and 
 Media
DESCRIPTION:A one-year teaching appointment in the Faculty of Arts at the U
 niversity of Groningen\, covering courses across the BA in Arts\, Culture 
 and Media and the Popular Music and Sonic Cultures master's track. Teachin
 g spans audiovisual arts\, popular music and arts management at both under
 graduate and postgraduate level. This is a teaching-weighted post rather t
 han a research one\, so it suits practitioners who want a formal academic 
 foothold in audiovisual and sonic culture without committing to a research
  track. REQUIREMENTS: a research master's in an appropriate arts disciplin
 e\, undergraduate teaching experience\, and English at C1 (CEFR). PREFERRE
 D: a PhD in an appropriate arts discipline\, a BKO or UTQ teaching qualifi
 cation\, postgraduate teaching experience\, musicology expertise\, Dutch a
 t B2\, and familiarity with the Dutch higher education system. Apply throu
 gh the AcademicTransfer posting (vacancy ID V26.2320-EN). Closes 15 August
  2026\; appointment starts 1 September 2026.\n\nOrganisation: University o
 f Groningen\, Faculty of Arts\nLocation: Groningen\, Netherlands (Broerstr
 aat 5)\nAward: EUR 3\,706 to 5\,760 gross per month at 1.0 FTE (the post i
 s 0.8 FTE)\, plus standard Dutch university holiday and year-end allowance
 s.\nDuration: Temporary\, 12-month fixed-term appointment at 0.8 FTE\, sta
 rting 1 September 2026\n\nMore: https://www.academictransfer.com/en/jobs/3
 62915/lecturer-4-arts-culture-and-media/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrant
 desk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.academictransfer.com/en/jobs/362915/lecturer-4-arts-culture
 -and-media/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Groningen\, Netherlands (Broerstraat 5)
END:VEVENT
