BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:unidee-cittadellarte-visiting-research-curator-2027-28@artificialnouvea
 u.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260831T203817Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260913
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260914
SUMMARY:Deadline: UNIDEE Residency Programs: Visiting Research Curator 2027
 -28
DESCRIPTION:Cittadellarte is recruiting a Visiting Research Curator to shap
 e the research arc of the UNIDEE Residency Modules for 2027-2028\, the rol
 e most recently held by Nina Fiocco and Gaia Martino. Founded by Michelang
 elo Pistoletto in 1999\, the residency has hosted thousands of artists and
  cultural professionals from 52 countries. WHAT THEY WANT: rather than a f
 ixed theme set in advance\, they want a curator who brings their own line 
 of inquiry and develops it collectively through the modules. Suggested the
 matic areas are the evolving landscape of socially engaged art practices\,
  research-driven and process-oriented practice\, and the conditions of cul
 tural work and cultural workers\, aligned with UNIDEE's focus on artistic 
 research in response to ecological\, geopolitical and technological challe
 nges. They also flag a specific interest in how contemporary art practices
  are archived\, drawing on the UNIDEE archive\, which documents over two d
 ecades of socially engaged art initiatives. THIS IS A JOB\, NOT A GRANT: t
 he duties list is long and operational. It covers proposing the overarchin
 g curatorial theme\, designing and delivering a minimum of 8 weekly reside
 ntial modules per year\, writing the curatorial statement and resident ope
 n call\, recruiting mentors and guests\, selecting residents\, hosting and
  facilitating every module in person\, communications and website texts\, 
 a dissemination strategy\, and conceiving and editing publications. There 
 is also teaching-adjacent work with the Unidee Academy of Contemporary Art
 s\, including public lectures and studio visits. Budget the time before ap
 plying. PROFILE: experience curating art in the public sphere and socially
  engaged art\, specialised knowledge of international contemporary art\, e
 xperience designing experimental and collaborative educational activities\
 , and experience with artistic research and dissemination standards. Excel
 lent English required\; Italian welcome but not essential. APPLYING: onlin
 e form with a project proposal of maximum 5000 characters stating your vis
 ion for the modules programme and a development strategy including possibl
 e mentors and guests\, plus a CV\, a portfolio of maximum three relevant p
 rojects\, and TWO LETTERS OF RECOMMENDATION\, so line up your referees ear
 ly. A jury of the UNIDEE Advisory Board\, the Director of Cittadellarte an
 d invited experts decides. They do not give feedback on unsuccessful propo
 sals.\n\nOrganisation: Fondazione Pistoletto Cittadellarte and UNIDEE Resi
 dency Programs\nLocation: Cittadellarte\, Biella\, Italy. Requires in-pers
 on presence at Cittadellarte for a minimum of one month plus the full leng
 th of each module.\nAward: Compensation and contractual terms commensurate
  with the candidate's level of professional experience\, starting from a g
 ross amount of EUR 22\,000 for the appointment\, excluding travel and hosp
 itality\, which are covered separately. No application fee.\nDuration: Tem
 porary appointment from November 2026 to December 2028\, covering the 2027
 -2028 research arc and a minimum of 8 residency modules per year. Deadline
  13 September 2026 at 23:59 CEST\; shortlisted candidates interviewed onli
 ne by mid-October 2026\, with the selected candidate announced a few days 
 later.\n\nMore: https://unidee.cittadellarte.it/activity.html?id=269&utm_s
 ource=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://unidee.cittadellarte.it/activity.html?id=269&utm_source=artific
 ialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Cittadellarte\, Biella\, Italy. Requires in-person presence at Cit
 tadellarte for a minimum of one month plus the full length of each module.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:pallas-projects-artist-initiated-projects-2027@artificialnouveau.github
 .io
DTSTAMP:20260831T203817Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261013
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261014
SUMMARY:Deadline: Pallas Projects/Studios: Artist-Initiated Projects 2027
DESCRIPTION:Annual programme of funded\, artist-initiated projects at Palla
 s Projects/Studios in Dublin\, aimed at early and mid-career artists\, eme
 rging artists and recent graduates. Up to six 4-week exhibitions between M
 arch and November 2027. WHAT MAKES IT DIFFERENT: the short-run\, quick-tur
 naround model is pitched explicitly as an alternative to the institutional
  route where studio visit to exhibition can take several years\, so the pr
 ogramme can respond to what artists are making now and reward experimentat
 ion and risk-taking. Solo\, two-person\, collaborative and group exhibitio
 ns are all considered\, across all contemporary visual art forms\, and wor
 k can be completed or in progress provided the outcomes are clearly expres
 sed. OUTREACH IS MANDATORY: proposals must include an outreach element aim
 ed at specific audiences or communities of interest\, such as events\, wor
 kshops\, talks\, performances or accompanying texts\, and there is a dedic
 ated EUR 330 budget for it. Gallery visits by colleges and local schools c
 an be arranged\, and artists are assisted in inviting curators and promoti
 ng the work. ELIGIBILITY\, three hard gates: you must be living and workin
 g in Ireland because the exhibitions are self-directed\; current undergrad
 uates are not accepted\; and you must not propose work that will be exhibi
 ted elsewhere in Dublin in 2027. NO AI: the call asks applicants not to us
 e AI to assist with the application\, and states that any instance must be
  declared. APPLYING: one PDF with a one-page proposal covering the outreac
 h aspect and target audiences\, a biography under 250 words\, up to 10 ima
 ges for individuals or 15 for groups clearly labelled and ideally mixing p
 revious and proposed work\, one video or audio link (two for groups)\, and
  a CV. Extra images or information will be discounted. An accessible alter
 native is offered: a maximum 6-minute video or voice recording covering th
 e same points. Selection is by the PP/S curator and directors\, dates are 
 offered rather than chosen so flexibility is expected\, and no feedback is
  given.\n\nOrganisation: Pallas Projects/Studios\nLocation: Pallas Project
 s/Studios\, Dublin\, Ireland. Applicants must be living and working in Ire
 land.\nAward: Solo exhibitions total EUR 2\,930: an artist fee of EUR 2\,0
 00\, a materials and installation budget of EUR 600\, and an outreach budg
 et of EUR 330. Two-person and group exhibitions total EUR 3\,930\, with th
 e artist fee rising to EUR 3\,000 and the other two budgets unchanged. All
  associated gallery costs are covered separately\, including rental\, insu
 rance\, invigilation\, printed and online ads\, publicity and sponsored so
 cial media\, curatorial support\, and professional photographic and video 
 documentation. No application fee.\nDuration: Up to six 4-week exhibitions
  running between March and November 2027. Deadline 5pm on Tuesday 13 Octob
 er 2026\; an online Q&A with curator and programme producer Eve Woods is s
 cheduled for 15 September 2026\, with questions submitted on registration.
 \n\nMore: https://pallasprojects.org/artist-initiated-projects-open-call?u
 tm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://pallasprojects.org/artist-initiated-projects-open-call?utm_sour
 ce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Pallas Projects/Studios\, Dublin\, Ireland. Applicants must be liv
 ing and working in Ireland.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:vcca-anne-spencer-fellowship-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260831T203817Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260915
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260916
SUMMARY:Deadline: VCCA Anne Spencer Fellowship 2027
DESCRIPTION:Named fellowship at VCCA's Mt. San Angelo campus in rural Virgi
 nia\, established in 2017 in honour of Harlem Renaissance poet and civil r
 ights activist Anne Spencer. It funds a one-month residency plus a USD 1\,
 500 honorarium for writers\, visual artists and composers of African Ameri
 can descent. WHAT YOU GET: private bedroom with private bath\, a separate 
 individual studio away from the bedroom\, and three meals a day\, inside a
  cross-disciplinary community of resident artists\, so the entire cost of 
 being there is carried by VCCA and the honorarium is on top of it. THE ONE
  CATCH ON ELIGIBILITY THIS CYCLE: the fellowship is described as open to w
 riters\, visual artists and composers\, but the 2027 application details n
 arrow the current round to WRITERS\, with preference given to those of Afr
 ican American descent. Read that as a writing-focused cycle rather than an
  open call to all three disciplines. COMMUNITY COMMITMENT: Anne Spencer Fe
 llows tour the Anne Spencer House and Garden Museum in Lynchburg and take 
 part in one Lynchburg-community activity\, choosing between a public prese
 ntation\, a workshop at an Anne Spencer partner school\, or another commun
 ity-based activity coordinated with the Anne Spencer Memorial Foundation. 
 Budget time for this\; it is not optional. HOW TO APPLY: there is no stand
 alone form. Complete the 'Application for Mt. San Angelo Residencies\, VCC
 A in Virginia\, Summer 2027' and select your fellowship interest at Questi
 on 2. A USD 30 application fee applies. Residency dates are drawn from 1 M
 ay to 31 August 2027 and decisions land by 31 December 2026.\n\nOrganisati
 on: Virginia Center for the Creative Arts (VCCA)\nLocation: Mt. San Angelo
 \, Amherst\, Virginia\, United States\, with activities in the nearby Lync
 hburg community.\nAward: USD 1\,500 honorarium paid on completion of the r
 esidency\, on top of a fully funded one-month stay: a private bedroom with
  private bath\, a separate individual studio and three meals a day. Applic
 ation fee USD 30.\nDuration: One month\, scheduled inside the 1 May to 31 
 August 2027 window. Applications open 1 June 2026\, deadline 15 September 
 2026\, notification by 31 December 2026.\n\nMore: https://www.vcca.com/app
 ly/fully-funded-fellowships/anne-spencer-fellowship/?utm_source=artificial
 nouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.vcca.com/apply/fully-funded-fellowships/anne-spencer-fellow
 ship/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Mt. San Angelo\, Amherst\, Virginia\, United States\, with activit
 ies in the nearby Lynchburg community.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:vcca-germaine-poliakov-fellowship-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260831T203817Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260915
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260916
SUMMARY:Deadline: VCCA Germaine Poliakov Fellowship 2027
DESCRIPTION:An 18-day writing residency at le Moulin a Nef\, VCCA's site in
  the village of Auvillar in southwest France\, with a USD 1\,000 travel st
 ipend attached. The fellowship was established in 2022 by VCCA Fellow and 
 board member Sandell Morse in memory of Germaine Poliakov\, a WWII Resista
 nce worker who sheltered and cared for Jewish refugee children in a secret
  house in southwest France\, so the history of the region is bound up with
  the award itself. HARD ELIGIBILITY GATE: this is open ONLY to writers who
  are already VCCA Fellows\, meaning you must have completed a residency at
  VCCA in Virginia before you can apply. If you have never been to Mt. San 
 Angelo\, this one is closed to you for now and the route in is the Virgini
 a application first. HOW TO APPLY: there is no separate form. Complete the
  'Moulin a Nef Residencies\, VCCA in France 2027' application and indicate
  your fellowship interest in the follow-up to Question 15. A USD 30 applic
 ation fee applies. Residency dates are drawn from a long window running 15
  March to 9 December 2027\, and notification is by 15 December 2026\, so p
 lan on a roughly 15-month lead time between applying and the latest possib
 le stay.\n\nOrganisation: Virginia Center for the Creative Arts (VCCA)\nLo
 cation: le Moulin a Nef\, Auvillar\, France\, VCCA's residency site in Gas
 cony.\nAward: USD 1\,000 travel stipend on top of a fully funded 18-day re
 sidency at le Moulin a Nef. Application fee USD 30.\nDuration: 18 days\, s
 cheduled inside the 15 March to 9 December 2027 window. Applications open 
 1 June 2026\, deadline 15 September 2026\, notification by 15 December 202
 6.\n\nMore: https://www.vcca.com/apply/fully-funded-fellowships/germaine-p
 oliakov-fellowship/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=refer
 ral
URL:https://www.vcca.com/apply/fully-funded-fellowships/germaine-poliakov-f
 ellowship/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:le Moulin a Nef\, Auvillar\, France\, VCCA's residency site in Gas
 cony.
END:VEVENT
